s rm -f, so acceptable. Since \"run everything yourself exactly as YAML runs it\" favors it.\n\nLet's inspect append gateway expected projection. Perhaps easiest create config, then invoke config event via the workflow's node script. We need artifact dir path. Use relative). Need create dirs via mkdir, which writes inside lineage, okay.\n\nNeed maybe `deep-review-audit-ledger` and effect ledger already provisioned; gateway may need ledger from these. It should find run directory's ledgers? Let's inspect mode-append-gateway resolution. Also might be no state log yet, so gateway opens it.\n\nLet's create config and strategy using template via node? We can write files with write tool. But first emit BINDING lines. The prompt requires BINDING before any writes. Let's do now in assistant message as text? It says emit to stdout. We haven't emitted. We can include in commentary now, and then write. Need exact order.\n\nBINDING: target=specs/system-speckit/spec-folder-tooling/005-subtrack-proposal-and-archive-reach\nBINDING: maxIterations=5\nBINDING: convergence=0.1\nBINDING: mode=review\nBINDING: dimensions=correctness,security,traceability,maintainability\nBINDING: specFolder=specs/system-speckit/spec-folder-tooling/005-subtrack-proposal-and-archive-reach\n\nDo that now, then create config/strategy maybe via write. Need not run resolve root.\n\nBut first maybe check if steer.md appears. Not yet. We'll check each iteration.\n\nBefore writing, also need perhaps gate / repo rules. We're a child dispatch bound to lineage, written authority. AGENTS says Gate 3 pre-resolved, Gate 5 repo rules? First write in session. Need read REPO RULES.md? There is likely root. But user said no stop-and-ask, record conflict and continue. We can comply by reading. At repo root? `REPO RULES.md`. Check. Also skills routing? We are @deep-review leaf, instructions explicitly say no nested. We don't need load skill tool because persona already. But artifact trigger says before first .md write route