{"type":"tool_result","callId":"chatcmpl-tool-a346b68d9f7ed664","status":"completed","result":"=== spec status ===\n16:    recent_action: \"Applied the 2026-11-14 plan verification to phases 006 to 010\"\n17:    next_safe_action: \"Start phase 006-relocate-resume-and-preflight\"\n51:| **Status** | Complete |\n72:> **Phase-parent note:** This spec.md is the ONLY authored document at the parent level. All detailed planning, task breakdowns, checklists, and decisions live in the child phase folders listed in the Phase Documentation Map below. This keeps the parent from drifting stale as phases execute and pivot.\n82:- Build `suggest-subtracks.mjs`, a read-only tool that proposes a whole-track subtrack map for a flat track and names the best-fitting subtrack for a new packet.\n87:- Close the in-scope findings of the two code reviews of 2026-11-14, in phases 006 to 010: reviewer A findings 1 to 12 and reviewer B findings 6, 7 and 8.\n89:### Operator Decisions\n97:- The review findings of 2026-11-14 are closed in new child phases 006 onward under this parent. Phases 001 to 005 stay Complete and are not edited. `recommend-level.sh` returned Level 1 for four of the five new phases and Level 0 for one, which the authoring card maps to Level 1. This is decision Q010 in `decision-record.md`.\n100:- Amendment of 2026-11-14 to phase 001: phase 008 adds exit status 3 to `relocate.mjs`, for a run whose steps and sweep all passed and whose only failure is a moved packet's own validation. It amends REQ-001, which says 2 on any failure, and REQ-012, which says a failure leaves the report and exits 2, both in `001-relocation-engine/spec.md`. Phase 001 stays Complete and is not edited, so this line is the record. Statuses 0, 1 and 2 keep their meaning otherwise.\n102:### Handed to the 008 session\n103:Reviewer B findings 1 to 5 concern the hub vocabulary packet, which lives on another session's branch. They are handed to the 008 command surfacing session by decision Q013 and are not planned here.\n122:| File Path | Change Type | Phase | Description |\n128:| `runtime/cli/spec/suggest-subtracks.mjs` | Create | 002 | Read-only proposal tool |\n138:| `runtime/cli/spec/relocate.mjs` | Modify | 006, 007, 008 | Resume and preflight state, bare-name and pre-archive rewrites, one added exit status |\n139:| `runtime/cli/spec/archive.sh`, `runtime/cli/spec/create.sh`, `runtime/cli/spec/README.md` | Modify | 008 | Restore verdict, mixed-track refusal, phase numbering that reads `z_archive/`, the exit codes stated in the `relocate.mjs` row |\n140:| `runtime/cli/retrieval/rg-wrapper.mjs`, `runtime/cli/spec/suggest-subtracks.mjs` | Modify | 009 | Archived marker in the path record, proposals the preflight accepts |\n141:| `graph-metadata.json`, and the advisor's generated `skill-graph.json` and `scorer-eval-baseline.json` | Modify | 009 | Reworded archive-search and sub-track signals, regenerated by the advisor's writers |\n142:| `runtime/cli/tests/relocate.vitest.ts`, `archive-track.vitest.ts`, `archive-numbering.vitest.ts`, `rg-include-archive.vitest.ts`, `suggest-subtracks.vitest.ts` | Modify | 006 to 009 | One happy-path case and one edge case per changed surface |\n143:| `runtime/cli/tests/relocate-real-pipeline.vitest.ts` | Create | 010 | A suite that runs the true writers |\n153:| Phase | Folder | Focus | Status |\n156:| 2 | 002-subtrack-proposal/ | `suggest-subtracks.mjs` and the wording and docs that raise a subtrack as a choice | Complete. Code in `b8912b831c` |\n159:| 5 | 005-tests-and-closeout/ | Vitest suites for phases 1 to 4, real-tree checks and packet closeout | Complete. Suites in `5fefd819e1` and `36b3a68ab7`. Ten criteria `Met`, AC-008 `Superseded` by ADR-001 |\n160:| 6 | 006-relocate-resume-and-preflight/ | A rerun of the same map finishes any stopped step, and the preflight refuses a source that never existed and two spellings of one folder. Closes A1, A3, A4, A5 and B6 | Complete |\n161:| 7 | 007-phase-map-and-prearchive-rewrites/ | Bare sibling names in a phase parent's documents and the id a packet had before it was archived are rewritten. Closes A2 and A8 | Complete |\n162:| 8 | 008-restore-and-phase-numbering/ | The restore verdict, the mixed-track refusal on restore and phase numbering that counts archived phases. Closes A6, A7 and A9 | Complete |\n163:| 9 | 009-proposal-search-and-routing/ | The archived marker in the path record, proposals the preflight accepts and two advisor signals. Closes A11, A12, B7 and B8 | Complete |\n164:| 10 | 010-real-pipeline-tests/ | One suite that runs the true writers and the resume paths. Closes A10 | Complete |\n166:### Phase Transition Rules\n173:### Phase Handoff Criteria\n178:| 002-subtrack-proposal | 003-subtrack-archive-and-numbering | `suggest-subtracks.mjs` emits a map in the `relocate.mjs` format and writes nothing | `git status --porcelain` prints nothing after a run |\n181:| 005-tests-and-closeout | 006-relocate-resume-and-preflight | The two reviews of 2026-11-14 are stored in `scratch/` and each in-scope finding is assigned to one phase | `ls scratch/review-20261114-*.md` lists two files |\n182:| 006-relocate-resume-and-preflight | 007-phase-map-and-prearchive-rewrites | After a late step fails once, a rerun of the same map finishes it | In a `mktemp` copy the second `relocate.mjs --apply` exits 0 and the third prints `relocate: nothing to do` |\n183:| 007-phase-map-and-prearchive-rewrites | 008-restore-and-phase-numbering | A renumbered phase is named correctly in its parent's documents | After `relocate.mjs --renumber <phase parent> --apply`, `rg` for the old folder name in the parent's `spec.md` prints nothing |\n184:| 008-restore-and-phase-numbering | 009-proposal-search-and-routing | A new phase is numbered above an archived one | With `001-alpha` live and `z_archive/002-gamma` archived, `create.sh --phase --parent` creates `003-*` |\n185:| 009-proposal-search-and-routing | 010-real-pipeline-tests | The path record marks archived paths and a 