{"type":"thinking","text":"The grep command searched dist and got huge; need targeted reading. Changelog itself is stale: says current release only phase 001-005, but phases 006-010 done. It includes \"A stopped --renumber run does not finish on a rerun\" which may still be true? Phase 006 explicitly excludes renumber resume (goal log residual). So maybe not stale. But changelog version 2.13.0.0 describes release not updated for remediation? Could be expected docs stale. It says \"The full suite passed after the review fixes ... 2567 passed\" while actual 2603. Maybe changelog was from phase 005 and not updated for 006-010. This likely major traceability finding.\n\nFeature catalog files likely stale. Need inspect per-feature files for behaviors and compare to code. The focus says \"changelog, feature catalog, playbook and README were never updated\". We need high-yield. Need findings likely multiple:\n1. Changelog v2.13.0.0 says 2603? Actually 2567 vs actual 2603; and doesn't mention exit 3, resume, mixed-track restore refusal, pre-archive rewrite, phase-map rewrites, archivedPaths, suggest non-NNN rejection. Some details contradictory: \"A stopped `--renumber` run does not finish on a rerun...\" is explicitly out of scope, but still maybe residual. The changelog says \"A map that stopped part-way finishes on next run\", phase 006 implemented. Could be true.\n2. `feature-catalog/tooling-and-scripts/spec-packet-relocation.md` likely missing exit 3, resume ledger, bare-name rewrites, pre-archive, case-folded duplicate, mixed-track restore.\n3. `feature-catalog/retrieval/rg-archive-search.md` likely missing `archivedPaths`.\n4. `feature-catalog/tooling-and-scripts/sub-track-proposal.md` likely missing non-NNN slug refusal.\n5. `manual-testing-playbook/tooling-and-scripts/spec-packet-relocation.md` likely manual scenarios stale.\n6. `manual-testing-playbook/retrieval/rg-archive-search.md` missing archivedPaths.\n7. `manual-testing-playbook/tooling-and-scripts/sub-track-proposal.md` missing non-NNN refusal.\n8. README root lines 416-417? root README high-level may need mention? User says highest yield docs stale against phases 006-010, which SKILL.md, references, changelog, feature catalog, playbook and README were never updated for. It implies there are gaps in each. But perhaps \"SKILL.md, references\" were updated? Need inspect.\n\nNeed ensure findings true and actionable. We should use actual code behavior. Let's read relevant source sections fully with line numbers, and docs. Also phase docs (child plans/goals) define exact intended behavior; use them to establish spec mismatch. Since review target is packet scope = manifest changes, documentation alignment. We can cite child goal/plan for intended behavior as context evidence.\n\nLet's read phase 006-010 goals/plans relevant sections, and code."}
{"type":"tool_call","callId":"chatcmpl-tool-9aeca2bab0bc8cb1","tool":"bash","input":{"command":"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Skilled; for p in 006-relocate-resume-and-preflight 007-phase-map-and-prearchive-rewrites 008-restore-and-phase-numbering 009-proposal-search-and-routing 010-real-pipeline-tests; do echo \"========== $p goal ==========\"; sed -n '/## 1. DURABLE DIRECTIVE/,/## 3. COMPLETION/p' specs/system-speckit/spec-folder-tooling/005-subtrack-proposal-and-archive-reach/$p/goal.md | head -100; done","description":"Read phase 006-010 durable directives"}}
{"type":"tool_result","callId":"chatcmpl-tool-9aeca2bab0bc8cb1","status":"completed","result":"========== 006-relocate-resume-and-preflight goal ==========\n## 1. DURABLE DIRECTIVE\n\n**Objective:** Make a rerun of the same relocation map finish any step that stopped the first run, and make the preflight refuse a source that never existed and two spellings of one folder.\n\n### Decisions\n\nFrozen choices. Changing one is an amendment.\n\n| ID | Decision |\n|----|----------|\n| D1 | The exit status of `relocate.mjs` keeps its three meanings: 0 nothing left to do, 1 work found on a dry run, 2 a refusal or a failed step. Phase 008 amends this for one case of the close. |\n| D2 | Every finding is reproduced in a `mktemp` copy before its fix. No run touches the real `specs/` tree. |\n| D3 | A finished map still ends on `relocate: nothing to do` with exit 0. |\n| D4 | No code comment names a spec path, a packet number or a finding id. |\n| D5 | A rerun repeats the close only until the sweep has passed once. A moved packet's own validation verdict is printed by every run that reaches the close and never keeps the map open. |\n\n<!-- /ANCHOR:directive -->\n\n---\n\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:completion -->\n## 3. COMPLETION CRITERIA\n========== 007-phase-map-and-prearchive-rewrites goal ==========\n## 1. DURABLE DIRECTIVE\n\n**Objective:** Leave no document naming a moved folder by a name it no longer has, after a phase is renumbered or re-parented and after a packet is restored from `z_archive/` onto a new number.\n\n### Decisions\n\nFrozen choices. Changing one is an amendment.\n\n| ID | Decision |\n|----|----------|\n| D1 | A bare folder name is rewritten only inside the parent folder of a phase whose parent is unchanged, and only where no letter, digit, underscore or hyphen stands before it. It is never matched across `specs/`, and `session_id` values stay as written. |\n| D2 | A dry run prints every rewrite the apply will make. |\n| D3 | The pre-archive id is rewritten only when the destination is not under `z_archive/` and no live folder holds it. |\n| D4 | Every finding is reproduced in a `mktemp` copy before its fix, and no code comment names a spec path, a packet number or a finding id. |\n| D5 | A re-parented phase's rows are removed from the old parent and added to the new one. The move is never refused over those rows, because re-parenting is a shipped capability. |\n\n<!-- /ANCHOR:directive -->\n\n---\n\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:completion -->\n## 3. COMPLETION CRITERIA\n========== 008-restore-and-phase-numbering goal ==========\n## 1. DURABLE DIRECTIVE\n\n**Objective:** Make an archive restore report what happened and never create a mixed track, and stop `create.sh` from giving a new phase the number of an archived one.\n\n### Decisions\n\nFrozen choices. Changing one is an amendment.\n\n| ID | Decision |\n|----|----------|\n| D1 | `relocate.mjs` gains one exit status, 3, for a run whose steps and sweep all passed and whose only failure is a moved packet's validation. Statuses 0, 1 and 2 keep their meaning otherwise. A run that ends on 3 has landed, so the same call again prints `relocate: nothing to do` and exits 0. This amends decision D1 of phase 006 for that one case, and REQ-001 and REQ-012 of phase 001, as the parent `spec.md` Operator Decisions record. |\n| D2 | A renumbering restore that ends on status 3 exits 0 and names the packet in a warning. |\n| D3 | `archive.sh` holds no copy of the sub-track predicate. It asks the relocate preflight and refuses a restore only on its mixed-track line. Every other preflight result leaves the restore as it is today. |\n| D4 | A new phase is numbered above every live and archived phase of its parent, and its predecessor is the highest live phase. |\n| D5 | Every finding is reproduced in a `mktemp` copy before its fix, and no code comment names a spec path, a packet number or a finding id. |\n\n<!-- /ANCHOR:directive -->\n\n---\n\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:completion -->\n## 3. COMPLETION CRITERIA\n========== 009-proposal-search-and-routing goal ==========\n## 1. DURABLE DIRECTIVE\n\n**Objective:** Mark archived paths in the JSON record of a path search, keep `suggest-subtracks.mjs` from printing a map the relocate preflight refuses, and make the archive-search and sub-track advisor signals match only the requests they were written for.\n\n### Decisions\n\nFrozen choices. Changing one is an amendment.\n\n| ID | Decision |\n|----|----------|\n| D1 | The `paths` field of the path record keeps its type. The archived marker is an added field. |\n| D2 | The advisor scorer is not changed in this phase. Signals change by wording only, and no signal added or reworded here contains a skill or track name. |\n| D3 | `skill-graph.json` and `scorer-eval-baseline.json` are regenerated by their writers after `origin/main` is taken into the branch, never edited or merged by hand, and every number that moves is listed in section 4. The hand-written `local-native-approved-divergences.json` is not edited: a new divergence stops the signal task. |\n| D4 | The code and the signals land as two commits. |\n| D5 | Every finding is reproduced before its fix, and no code comment names a spec path, a packet number or a finding id. |\n\n<!-- /ANCHOR:directive -->\n\n---\n\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:completion -->\n## 3. COMPLETION CRITERIA\n========== 010-real-pipeline-tests goal ==========\n## 1. DURABLE DIRECTIVE\n\n**Objective:** Add one suite that runs the relocation pipeline and a renumbering restore with the true writers, and that fails when a pipeline step is removed.\n\n### Decisions\n\nFrozen choices. Changing one is an amendment.\n\n| ID | Decision |\n|----|----------|\n| D1 | No script under test changes in this phase. A defect the suite exposes is recorded in section 4 and raised to the operator. |\n| D2 | The suite never writes to the real checkout. A writer that writes under its own location runs from a copy in the temp repository. |\n| D3 | Every assertion reads a value a true writer wrote. The two stubbed suites keep their stubs. |\n| D4 | The floor is one happy path and one edge case per surface. No case is added per branch. |\n| D5 | No code comment names a spec path, a packet number or a finding id. |\n\n<!-- /ANCHOR:directive -->\n\n---\n\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:completion -->\n## 3. COMPLETION CRITERIA\n"}
