{"type":"thinking","text":"Now identify exact doc gaps. Feature relocation says exit status: 0/1/2, no 3. That is clearly stale vs phase 008 D1. Great P1 traceability/correctness docs. Feature relocation \"The run is safe to repeat ... run that stopped on a failed step is finished by running same map again\" but doesn't mention late steps and resume, exit 3. We can make one finding about exit code 3 omitted. Maybe combine with \"nothing to do on status 3\" missing.\n\nFeature relocation list of refusals: \"source or destination named by two entries, a chain or swap\" but phase 006 specifically \"case-folded duplicate refusal\" maybe not mentioned. Code line 488 comment about folded case. Docs say \"two entries\" not case-folded. Need exact code and test. Could be an omission finding.\n\nFeature relocation \"What a move rewrites\" omits bare sibling names in phase parent docs and pre-archive id rewrite. It says old id matched as whole path, longer id left alone. But phase 007 adds bare-name rewrite; docs still only whole old id. Could be misleading/incomplete. Also \"phase parent's children_ids drops or adds\" etc. Need cite lines in feature doc. We'll get line numbers.\n\nFeature relocation source tests only relocate.vitest.ts, omits relocate-real-pipeline.vitest.ts and maybe new suites. Phase 010 created new suite. The source files table in feature catalog probably stale. Could be separate finding: missing new true-writer suite means catalog underreports validation. But scope maybe only docs.\n\nFeature archive search: says `paths` stays list of plain strings, but phase 009 D1 added archived marker as an added field `archivedPaths`. This is a direct omission; JSON path record doesn't mention archivedPaths. That's clearly P1 traceability. Cite docs line and code line 382. Also root README line 1205 mentions only archived search but not archivedPaths. System-spec-kit README line 332 same omission. Retrieval-conventions line 84 says structured/count rows carry archived, not path `archivedPaths`. User explicitly calls \"archivedPaths in path JSON\". We can make a cross-consumer finding with all docs affected. But each finding should cite primary file:line and scopeProof via grep. Could be P1 because completion criteria require JSON path record marks same paths. Documentation says \"paths list stays plain strings\" but fails to mention marker; arguably incomplete but not wrong. It says \"In JSON the report carries includeArchive: true, and each row in results and in counts carries archived... The paths list of path-only stays plain strings. Without flag none of these fields appear.\" That implies no archivedPaths; code adds it. This is a spec mismatch P1.\n\nFeature sub-track: doesn't mention non NNN-slug refusal. Code `proposeRetroactive` at 293-298 prints refusal and no map, exit 0. Phase 009 requirement likely says refuse non NNN-slug. Docs say \"The tool prints one explanatory line and no map when track grouped/fewer/no grouping\" and \"Archived packets not counted\". Missing case: misnamed packets. That's a doc gap P1 or P2. Completion criterion says suggest on flat track; but user focus says \"suggest-subtracks refusing non NNN-slug packets\" is a doc gap. Could be P2 documentation, but because docs assert a map for every flat track above threshold and no mention, a user may pass a map with invalid names? Actually tool prints no map; docs omit. P2 perhaps. We need P1 for CONDITIONAL? There may be stronger.\n\nPlaybook relocation: step 9 removes copy; expected after apply. It doesn't test exit 3 / resume, preflight duplicate case-fold, phase rewrite, renumber. It says scenario focuses dry run etc. The user focus says docs stale against phases 006-010. Could be P1 if manual playbook claims comprehensive but omits new behaviors? The manual playbook is supposed to cover relocation but only old scenario. However a manual test doesn't need cover every new behavior. Could be P2.\n\nChangelog: version 2.13.0.0 released before 006-010. It doesn't mention latter behaviors. But maybe changelog is for v2.13.0.0 and code changes after release are unreleased; should add next version entry, not edit. The manifest includes changelog v2.13.0.0.md. The focus explicitly says \"changelog ... never updated for phases 006-010\". A finding: changelog claims \"exit 0/1/2\" and \"A second --apply...\"; omits exit 3 and resume. It was never updated. But is editing old changelog wrong? Usually new version. Still doc stale if behavior changed within package. Need be careful: if release version wasn't bumped after post-release fixes, that's traceability. Could cite version 2.13.0.0 and no later changelog. Need list changelog dir."}
