{"type":"tool_result","callId":"chatcmpl-tool-88a09c0988ef1d64","status":"completed","result":"245:| 492 | Spec packet relocation and renumbering | [492](tooling-and-scripts/spec-packet-relocation.md) | [spec-packet-relocation](../feature-catalog/tooling-and-scripts/spec-packet-relocation.md) |\n246:| 495 | Spec validation of archived packets | [495](tooling-and-scripts/spec-validation-archive-reach.md) | [spec-validation-rule-engine](../feature-catalog/tooling-and-scripts/spec-validation-rule-engine.md) |\n249:| 493 | Sub-track proposal | [493](tooling-and-scripts/sub-track-proposal.md) | [sub-track-proposal](../feature-catalog/tooling-and-scripts/sub-track-proposal.md) |\n336:| 494 | Ripgrep archive search | [494](retrieval/rg-archive-search.md) | [rg-archive-search](../feature-catalog/retrieval/rg-archive-search.md) |\n=== feature root entries ===\n682:### Spec packet relocation\n690:`relocate.mjs` takes one mode: `--map`, `--from` with `--to`, `--renumber` or `--declare-subtrack`. It prints the plan and exits 1 when a dry run finds work, and `--apply` writes. Every refusal happens before the first write. An applied run moves the folders, rewrites references under `specs/`, re-derives the packets' recorded paths, refreshes the track roots, the relocation ledger, the redirect table and the trigger index, then closes with the track-root sweep and strict validation of each moved packet. Code and CI files are never rewritten: a moved path named there refuses the run.\n694:See [`tooling-and-scripts/spec-packet-relocation.md`](tooling-and-scripts/spec-packet-relocation.md) for full implementation and test file listings.\n730:### Sub-track proposal\n1070:### Ripgrep archive search\n"}
