{"type":"tool_result","callId":"chatcmpl-tool-9954fac5df2e99a9","status":"completed","result":"   260\t   - For sections without sufficient source context, write \"N/A - insufficient source context\" instead of fabricating content\n   261\t   - Run `check-placeholders.sh <spec-folder>` to verify zero placeholders remain (see level specifications reference for the full procedure)\n   262\t   - Document the level change in changelog\n   263\t2. **Uncertainty about level <80%** - Present level options to user, default to higher. When `AI_SESSION_CHILD=1` marks a non-interactive child, record the level question with the higher level as its default in the lineage directory and continue.\n   264\t3. **Template doesn't fit requirements** - Adapt closest template, document modifications\n   265\t4. **User requests skip (Option D)** - Warn about tech debt, explain debugging challenges, confirm consent. When `AI_SESSION_CHILD=1` marks a non-interactive child, record the skip request in the lineage directory with documentation kept as the default and continue.\n   266\t5. **Validation fails with errors** - Report specific failures, provide fix guidance, re-run after fixes\n   267\t\n   268\t---\n   269\t\n   270\t## 5. SUCCESS CRITERIA\n   271\t\n   272\tSuccess means the selected spec folder uses the right template set, placeholders and sample content are removed, links between packet docs work, continuity is saved or updated, Level 2+ `tasks.md` P0/P1 checklist items are verified with evidence, every `acceptance-criteria.md` criterion is `Met`, `Waived` or `Superseded`, and `validate.sh --strict` has no blocking errors.\n   273\t\n   274\t---\n   275\t\n   276\t## 6. INTEGRATION POINTS\n   277\t\n   278\tP0 blocks, P1 requires completion or approved deferral, and P2 is optional. Code updates route through `sk-code`; documentation updates route through `sk-doc`; git handoff routes through `sk-git`.\n   279\t\n   280\t### Quick Reference Commands\n   281\t\n   282\t| Command | Usage |\n   283\t| --- | --- |\n   284\t| Canonical intake | `/speckit:plan --intake-only \"Description\"` |\n   285\t| Create spec folder | `./runtime/cli/spec/create.sh \"Description\" --short-name name --level 2` |\n   286\t| Create in a track | Add `--track <track>` to the create command. The new packet is also listed in `specs/<track>/graph-metadata.json` |\n   287\t| Create in a sub-track | Add `--track <track>/<sub>` for a declared sub-track. Numbering restarts inside it, and `suggest-subtracks.mjs` names the best-fitting sub-track for a description |\n   288\t| Track-root lists | `node .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/refresh-track-roots.mjs --apply` after moving, renaming or deleting a packet in a track by hand; `archive.sh` refreshes it itself. The pre-push hook blocks a commit whose track lists other packets than it holds |\n   289\t| Validate | `.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/validate.sh specs/007-feature/` |\n   290\t| Verify code alignment drift | `python3 .skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-skilled/assets/scripts/verify_alignment_drift.py --root .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit` |\n   291\t| Save context | `node .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/dist/continuity/generate-context.js /tmp/save-context-data-<session-id>.json specs/007-feature/` |\n   292\t| Gate 1 trigger lookup | `node .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/retrieval/lookup-trigger-index.mjs --json -- \"<prompt>\"` (exit `0` hit, `1` no-hit, `2` broken) |\n   293\t| Regenerate trigger index | `node .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/retrieval/generate-trigger-index.mjs` |\n   294\t| Free-text retrieval | The ripgrep recipes in `references/retrieval/retrieval-conventions.md` §2, scoped by the trailing positional path |\n   295\t| Next spec number | `ls -d specs/[0-9]*/ \\| sed 's/.*\\/\\([0-9]*\\)-.*/\\1/' \\| sort -n \\| tail -1` |\n   296\t| Upgrade level | `bash .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/upgrade-level.sh specs/007-feature/ --to 2` |\n   297\t| Completeness | `.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/calculate-completeness.sh specs/007-feature/` |\n   298\t| Worktree isolation | `.skilled/bin/worktree-session.sh` creates a per-session git worktree with isolated `SPEC_KIT_DB_DIR` / `SPECKIT_IPC_SOCKET_DIR`. Pair with `worktree-reaper.sh` for teardown and `worktree-guard.sh` for lock enforcement |\n   299\t| Session cleanup | `.skilled/scripts/session-cleanup.sh` resolves PIDs across claude/opencode/opencode runtimes |\n   300\t\n   301\tCanonical command lifecycle:\n   302\t- `/speckit:plan --intake-only` establishes or repairs the packet when standalone intake is needed.\n   303\t- `/deep:research` follows `../system-deep-loop/deep-research/references/protocol/spec-check-protocol.md` when research needs bounded `spec.md` anchoring.\n   304\t- Either `/speckit:plan` or `/speckit:complete` continues from the same folder. It reuses the shared intake contract (`.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/workflows/intake-contract.md`) only when local `folder_state` still needs repair.\n   305\t- When intake runs, the returned `start_state` is the canonical downstream field.\n=== root README 400-435 ===\n   400\t\n   401\t#### Scripts and Validation\n   402\t\n   403\t`validate.sh` runs 42 rules against a spec folder and reports what passes and what needs fixing. Rules check required files, template compliance, placeholder detection, anchor markers and cross-reference consistency.\n   404\t\n   405\tEight of them only warn and never fail a run. Two of those are worth knowing. `FRONTMATTER_VALUES` checks each doc's `contextType` and `importance_tier` against the one value list in `.skilled/skills/sk-doc/sk-create-frontmatter/assets/frontmatter-values.json`. `SOURCE_TAGS` checks that the `[SOURCE: path:line]` tags in research and review artifacts point at a file and line that exist.\n   406\t\n   407\t**Spec management scripts** in `.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/`:\n   408\t\n   409\t- **`create.sh`** - create spec folders with level-appropriate templates. Use `--phase` for a parent with child phases\n   410\t- **`validate.sh`** - run 42 validation rules. Use `--recursive` for phase folders and `--quiet` for the result line only. A `--strict` run on a Draft packet whose only errors are derived metadata repairs it once and revalidates, so it can write files. `SPECKIT_DRAFT_AUTO_REPAIR=0` turns that off\n   411\t- **`upgrade-level.sh`** - upgrade a spec folder to a higher level by injecting new sections\n   412\t- **`recommend-level.sh`** - analyze scope and risk to recommend the right documentation level\n   413\t- **`calculate-completeness.sh`** - calculate spec folder completeness as a percentage\n   414\t- **`check-completion.sh`** - verify all completion criteria are met\n   415\t- **`check-placeholders.sh`** - find remaining `[PLACEHOLDER]` values after level upgrade\n   416\t- **`relocate.mjs`** - move, renumber or re-parent spec packets and rewrite every store that records the path. Takes `--map <file.json>`, `--from` with `--to`, `--renumber <folder>` or `--declare-subtrack <track>/<name>`. Dry run by default, `--apply` writes\n   417\t- **`suggest-subtracks.mjs`** - propose a whole-track sub-track map for a flat track, or with `--describe` name the declared sub-track a new packet fits best. Writes nothing\n   418\t\n   419\t**`validate.sh` exit codes**\n   420\t\n   421\t| Exit | Meaning |\n   422\t| --- | --- |\n   423\t| **0** | All rules pass. Ready to proceed |\n   424\t| **1** | User error (bad flags or invalid input) |\n   425\t| **2** | Validation error. Must fix before claiming completion |\n   426\t| **3** | System error (file I/O failure, missing manifest or other environment problem) |\n   427\t\n   428\t**Useful flags and behaviors**\n   429\t\n   430\t`--verbose` shows details behind each rule. `--recursive` validates a parent and all child phase folders. `--include-archive` works only with `--recursive` and also validates the packets in the `z_archive/` of the folder given and, for a track root, of each declared sub-track. `validate.sh` implements no rules itself. It hands every rule decision to a single Node orchestrator.\n   431\t\n   432\tThe default scaffold path skips post-create validation. Set `SPECKIT_POST_VALIDATE=1` to enable it for strict CI workflows. Path traversal inputs, for example a `--path` value that climbs above the reposi","truncated":true}
{"type":"tool_call","callId":"chatcmpl-tool-977a7ce937f58c69","tool":"bash","input":{"command":"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Skilled; echo '=== archive code restore section ==='; nl -ba .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/archive.sh | sed -n '340,455p'; nl -ba .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/archive.sh | sed -n '720,785p'; echo '=== relocate casefold/refusal ==='; nl -ba .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/relocate.mjs | sed -n '480,570p'; echo '=== relocate status 3 ==='; nl -ba .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/relocate.mjs | sed -n '1635,1675p'","description":"Read archive restore and relocate refusal code"}}
{"type":"tool_result","callId":"chatcmpl-tool-977a7ce937f58c69","status":"completed","result":"=== archive code restore section ===\n   340\t    [[ -f \"$cache\" ]] || return 0\n   341\t    if [[ ! -f \"$discovery_module\" ]]; then\n   342\t        log_warning \"descriptions.json was not refreshed: $discovery_module is missing. Restore it, then run ensureDescriptionCache.\"\n   343\t        return 0\n   344\t    fi\n   345\t    if ! command -v node >/dev/null 2>&1; then\n   346\t        log_warning \"descriptions.json was not refreshed: node is not on PATH, so $discovery_module cannot run. Restore node, then run ensureDescriptionCache.\"\n   347\t        return 0\n   348\t    fi\n   349\t    if ! node --input-type=module -e '\n   350\timport { pathToFileURL } from \"node:url\";\n   351\tconst { ensureDescriptionCache } = await import(pathToFileURL(process.argv[1]).href);\n   352\tif (ensureDescriptionCache([process.argv[2]]) === null) process.exit(1);\n   353\t' \"$discovery_module\" \"$specs_root\" >/dev/null; then\n   354\t        log_warning \"descriptions.json may still list the old folder. Rerun ensureDescriptionCache on $specs_root.\"\n   355\t    fi\n   356\t}\n   357\t\n   358\t# A restore is refused when the relocation preflight for the same move reports\n   359\t# that its destination would leave a flat packet beside sub-tracks. The rule\n   360\t# lives in the preflight, so this asks for a dry run of that move and reads only\n   361\t# this one verdict; a dirty tree, a taken number and every other preflight\n   362\t# answer stay with the restore's own checks.\n   363\trefuse_mixed_track_restore() {\n   364\t    local archived=\"$1\"\n   365\t    local destination=\"$2\"\n   366\t    local specs_root=\"$3\"\n   367\t    local relocate_script=\"$SCRIPT_DIR/relocate.mjs\"\n   368\t    local from_id to_id track track_dir sub sub_id preflight name\n   369\t    local status=0\n   370\t\n   371\t    [[ -f \"$relocate_script\" ]] || return 0\n   372\t    track=\"$(track_of \"$destination\" \"$specs_root\")\"\n   373\t    # A packet already inside a sub-track has no track level above it that could\n   374\t    # become mixed, so the preflight has no mixed-track verdict to give.\n   375\t    [[ -n \"$track\" && \"$track\" != */* ]] || return 0\n   376\t\n   377\t    from_id=\"${archived#\"$specs_root\"/}\"\n   378\t    to_id=\"${destination#\"$specs_root\"/}\"\n   379\t    # set -e would end the script on every non-zero preflight exit, including\n   380\t    # \"work found\" and a plain refusal, so the status is captured with the\n   381\t    # output. Only the mixed-track line below decides.\n   382\t    preflight=\"$(node \"$relocate_script\" --from \"$from_id\" --to \"$to_id\" 2>&1)\" || status=$?\n   383\t    [[ \"$preflight\" == *\"would hold flat packets\"* ]] || return 0\n   384\t\n   385\t    track_dir=\"$specs_root/$track\"\n   386\t    for sub in \"$track_dir\"/*/; do\n   387\t        sub=\"${sub%/}\"\n   388\t        if is_declared_subtrack \"$sub\" \"$specs_root\"; then\n   389\t            sub_id=\"${sub#\"$specs_root\"/}\"\n   390\t            break\n   391\t        fi\n   392\t    done\n   393\t    name=\"$(basename \"$to_id\")\"\n   394\t    log_error \"Restore refused: track specs/$track would hold flat packets. Move the packet into a sub-track instead: node $relocate_script --from $from_id --to ${sub_id:-$track/<sub>}/$name --apply\"\n   395\t    exit 1\n   396\t}\n   397\t\n   398\t# The next number after every one already used in a packet home, live or\n   399\t# archived, so the restored packet cannot collide with either. relocate.mjs then\n   400\t# moves it and rewrites every record that names it, from its own preflight on.\n   401\trestore_on_next_number() {\n   402\t    local archived=\"$1\"\n   403\t    local home=\"$2\"\n   404\t    local archive_dir=\"$3\"\n   405\t    local name=\"$4\"\n   406\t    local specs_root=\"$5\"\n   407\t    local holder=\"$6\"\n   408\t    local relocate_script=\"$SCRIPT_DIR/relocate.mjs\"\n   409\t    local highest=0 candidate number next from_id to_id home_id\n   410\t\n   411\t    for candidate in \"$home\"/[0-9][0-9][0-9]-*/ \"$archive_dir\"/[0-9][0-9][0-9]-*/; do\n   412\t        [[ -d \"${candidate%/}\" ]] || continue\n   413\t        number=\"$(basename \"${candidate%/}\")\"\n   414\t        number=\"${number:0:3}\"\n   415\t        if (( 10#$number > highest )); then\n   416\t            highest=$((10#$number))\n   417\t        fi\n   418\t    done\n   419\t    next=\"$(printf '%03d' $((highest + 1)))\"\n   420\t\n   421\t    from_id=\"${archived#\"$specs_root\"/}\"\n   422\t    home_id=\"${home#\"$specs_root\"}\"\n   423\t    home_id=\"${home_id#/}\"\n   424\t    to_id=\"${next}-${name:4}\"\n   425\t    [[ -z \"$home_id\" ]] || to_id=\"$home_id/$to_id\"\n   426\t\n   427\t    if [[ ! -f \"$relocate_script\" ]]; then\n   428\t        log_error \"Number ${name:0:3} is taken by $holder and $relocate_script is missing, so the packet cannot take number $next\"\n   429\t        exit 1\n   430\t    fi\n   431\t    log_info \"Number ${name:0:3} is taken by $holder; restoring as specs/$to_id\"\n   432\t    # set -e would end the script on a failed node call, hiding the one status\n   433\t    # that still means the move landed. Capture it so that verdict can be told\n   434\t    # apart from a run whose steps did not finish.\n   435\t    local status=0\n   436\t    node \"$relocate_script\" --from \"$from_id\" --to \"$to_id\" --apply || status=$?\n   437\t    if [[ \"$status\" -eq 3 ]]; then\n   438\t        log_success \"Restored: $archived -> $specs_root/$to_id\"\n   439\t        log_warning \"Restored packet $specs_root/$to_id failed its own validation; the move is complete, but the packet still needs attention. Read the close validate line above.\"\n   440\t        exit 0\n   441\t    fi\n   442\t    if [[ \"$status\" -ne 0 ]]; then\n   443\t        log_error \"Restore did not finish. Read the report above, then rerun: node $relocate_script --from $from_id --to $to_id --apply\"\n   444\t        exit 1\n   445\t    fi\n   446\t    log_success \"Restored: $archived -> $specs_root/$to_id\"\n   447\t}\n   448\t\n   449\t# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n   450\t# 4. CORE FUNCTIONS\n   451\t# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n   452\t\n   453\tget_completeness() {\n   454\t    local spec_folder=\"$1\"\n   455\t\n   720\t    destination=\"$home/$basename\"\n   721\t    track=\"$(track_of \"$destination\" \"$specs_root\")\"\n   722\t\n   723\t    # The home comes from the physical archive path and was checked as a packet\n   724\t    # home above. Checking the resolved home again keeps the move inside the specs\n   725\t    # root if that derivation ever changes, and a link at the target is refused\n   726\t    # rather than followed.\n   727\t    if ! is_path_within \"$(resolve_existing_dir \"$home\")\" \"$specs_root\"; then\n   728\t        log_error \"Restore destination resolves outside the specs root $specs_root: $destination\"\n   729\t        exit 1\n   730\t    fi\n   731\t\n   732\t    local logical_archived=\"$archived_folder\"\n   733\t    [[ \"$logical_archived\" == /* ]] || logical_archived=\"$PROJECT_ROOT/$logical_archived\"\n   734\t    reject_linked_argument \"$logical_archived\" \"$specs_root\" \"Restore\"\n   735\t\n   736\t    # A folder or link already at the exact destination is refused: two live\n   737\t    # packets under one name is a decision for a person, not a renumber.\n   738\t    if [[ -e \"$destination\" || -L \"$destination\" ]]; then\n   739\t        log_error \"Restore target already exists: $destination\"\n   740\t        exit 1\n   741\t    fi\n   742\t\n   743\t    # Both restore paths move the folder from here on, so the mixed-track\n   744\t    # verdict is read before either one starts.\n   745\t    refuse_mixed_track_restore \"$resolved_archived\" \"$destination\" \"$specs_root\"\n   746\t\n   747\t    # A packet number names one folder among its siblings. When a live packet\n   748\t    # under another name already holds the restored packet's number, the packet\n   749\t    # takes the next free number instead. A new number changes every record that\n   750\t    # names the packet, so the relocation engine moves it rather than mv.\n   751\t    local number_holder=\"\"\n   752\t    local sibling\n   753\t    for sibling in \"$home\"/\"${basename:0:3}\"-*/; do\n   754\t        if [[ -d \"${sibling%/}\" ]]; then\n ","truncated":true}
