{"type":"tool_result","callId":"chatcmpl-tool-a69b664314feee0b","status":"completed","result":"   674\t`create.sh`, `recommend-level.sh`, `upgrade-level.sh`, `calculate-completeness.sh`, `check-completion.sh` and `archive.sh` are the entry points. `create.sh` counts archived numbers when it numbers a packet and, with `--track`, prints at most one advisory sub-track line from `suggest-subtracks.mjs`. `archive.sh` archives into the `z_archive/` beside the packet, a declared sub-track's own included, refreshes the description cache after a move and restores a packet whose number is taken onto the next free number through `relocate.mjs`.\n   675\t\n   676\t#### Source Files\n   677\t\n   678\tSee [`tooling-and-scripts/spec-lifecycle-automation.md`](tooling-and-scripts/spec-lifecycle-automation.md) for full implementation and test file listings.\n   679\t\n   680\t---\n   681\t\n   682\t### Spec packet relocation\n   683\t\n   684\t#### Description\n   685\t\n   686\tMoves, renumbers and re-parents spec packets and rewrites every store that records the packet path, as a dry run unless --apply is passed.\n   687\t\n   688\t#### Current Reality\n   689\t\n   690\t`relocate.mjs` takes one mode: `--map`, `--from` with `--to`, `--renumber` or `--declare-subtrack`. It prints the plan and exits 1 when a dry run finds work, and `--apply` writes. Every refusal happens before the first write. An applied run moves the folders, rewrites references under `specs/`, re-derives the packets' recorded paths, refreshes the track roots, the relocation ledger, the redirect table and the trigger index, then closes with the track-root sweep and strict validation of each moved packet. Code and CI files are never rewritten: a moved path named there refuses the run.\n   691\t\n   692\t#### Source Files\n   693\t\n   694\tSee [`tooling-and-scripts/spec-packet-relocation.md`](tooling-and-scripts/spec-packet-relocation.md) for full implementation and test file listings.\n   695\t\n   696\t---\n   697\t\n   698\t### Spec validation rule engine\n   699\t\n   700\t#### Description\n   701\t\n   702\tValidation orchestrator that detects spec level, loads configured or alphabetical rule scripts, applies severity policy, supports recursive phase validation, and emits human-readable or JSON results.\n   703\t\n   704\t#### Current Reality\n   705\t\n   706\t`validate.sh` is the authoritative completion gate; a stale compiled orchestrator makes it exit 3 with no rule output rather than pass silently. `--recursive --include-archive` also validates the packets in the `z_archive/` of the folder given and, for a track root, of each declared sub-track.\n   707\t\n   708\t#### Source Files\n   709\t\n   710\tSee [`tooling-and-scripts/spec-validation-rule-engine.md`](tooling-and-scripts/spec-validation-rule-engine.md) for full implementation and test file listings.\n   711\t\n   712\t---\n   713\t\n   714\t### Strict validation add-ons: continuity freshness and evidence markers\n   715\t\n   716\t#### Description\n   717\t\n   718\tExtends `validate.sh --strict` with continuity-freshness, evidence-marker lint, bracket-depth audit tooling and the normalizer lint guardrail.\n   719\t\n   720\t#### Current Reality\n   721\t\n   722\t`--strict` selects which rules run; a warning is advice and does not fail the run.\n   723\t\n   724\t#### Source Files\n   725\t\n   726\tSee [`tooling-and-scripts/strict-validation-addons-continuity-freshness-and-evidence-markers.md`](tooling-and-scripts/strict-validation-addons-continuity-freshness-and-evidence-markers.md) for full implementation and test file listings.\n   727\t\n   728\t---\n   729\t\n   730\t### Sub-track proposal\n   731\t\n   732\t#### Description\n   733\t\n   734\tProposes a sub-track grouping for a whole flat track, or names the declared sub-track a new packet fits, and writes nothing.\n   735\t\n   736\t#### Current Reality\n   737\t\n   738\t`suggest-subtracks.mjs --track <name>` prints a JSON map of every live packet in a flat track to a proposed sub-track, in the shape `relocate.mjs --map` takes, or one line that says why there is no map. With `--describe` it prints the best-fitting declared sub-track or says that none fits. It reads packet metadata only and exits 0 for a proposal and for an explained non-answer.\n   739\t\n   740\t#### Source Files\n   741\t\n   742\tSee [`tooling-and-scripts/sub-track-proposal.md`](tooling-and-scripts/sub-track-proposal.md) for full implementation and test file listings.\n   743\t\n   744\t---\n   745\t\n   746\t### Template compliance contract enforcement\n   747\t\n   748\t#### Description\n  1062\t#### Current Reality\n  1063\t\n  1064\tThe structured recipe ranks matches first, then returns one highest-ranked row per file. The default limit is 20 files; --limit 0 is uncapped. JSON schema version 3 reports total matches and files, hidden files and matches, each shown row's moreInFile count, the effective limit and whether files were omitted. Human output reports the same totals and identifies additional matches in a shown file. The path-only and count recipes apply the same limit and report the files they hid.\n  1065\t\n  1066\t#### Source Files\n  1067\t\n  1068\tSee [retrieval/rg-flood-control.md](retrieval/rg-flood-control.md) for full implementation and test file listings.\n  1069\t\n  1070\t### Ripgrep archive search\n  1071\t\n  1072\t#### Description\n  1073\t\n  1074\tSearches archived packets on request, labels each archived hit and lists the archived packet metadata files that carry the phrase.\n  1075\t\n  1076\t#### Current Reality\n  1077\t\n  1078\tEvery recipe leaves `z_archive/` out by default. `rg-wrapper.mjs --include-archive` searches archived packets too. Human output marks each archived path `[archived]`, and JSON rows in `results` and `counts` carry `archived: true` or `archived: false`. A second lane lists the `description.json` and `graph-metadata.json` files of archived packets that match, under a `json    :` section in human output and as `jsonLane` in JSON, and it is not bounded by the file limit.\n  1079\t\n  1080\t#### Source Files\n  1081\t\n  1082\tSee [retrieval/rg-archive-search.md](retrieval/rg-archive-search.md) for full implementation and test file listings.\n  1083\t\n  1084\t---\n  1085\t\n  1086\t## 9. CONTEXT PRESERVATION\n  1087\t\n  1088\t### Session relaunch loop\n  1089\t\n  1090\t#### Description\n=== playbook root 235-255 ===\n   235\t| 243 | Setup, native module health and prerequisite validation | [243](tooling-and-scripts/setup-native-module-health-and-mcp-installation.md) | [setup-native-module-health-and-mcp-installation](../feature-catalog/tooling-and-scripts/setup-native-module-health-and-mcp-installation.md) |\n   236\t| 464 | Shared frontmatter value list | [464](tooling-and-scripts/shared-frontmatter-value-list.md) | [shared-frontmatter-value-list](../feature-catalog/tooling-and-scripts/shared-frontmatter-value-list.md) |\n   237\t| EX-041 | sk-git worktree convention | [EX-041](tooling-and-scripts/sk-git-worktree-convention.md) | [sk-git-worktree-convention](../feature-catalog/tooling-and-scripts/sk-git-worktree-convention.md) |\n   238\t| 150 | Source-dist alignment validation | [150](tooling-and-scripts/source-dist-alignment-validation.md) | [source-dist-alignment-enforcement](../feature-catalog/tooling-and-scripts/source-dist-alignment-enforcement.md) |\n   239\t| 465 | Source tag resolution | [465](tooling-and-scripts/source-tag-resolution.md) | [source-tag-resolution](../feature-catalog/tooling-and-scripts/source-tag-resolution.md) |\n   240\t| 242 | Spec-folder detection and description metadata | [242](tooling-and-scripts/spec-folder-detection-and-description.md) | [spec-folder-detection-and-description](../feature-catalog/tooling-and-scripts/spec-folder-detection-and-description.md) |\n   241\t| PHASE-008 | Spec-folder literal naming (CLI-driven slug) | [PHASE-008](tooling-and-scripts/spec-folder-literal-naming-cli-driven-slug.md) | [spec-folder-literal-naming-ai-derived-slugs](../feature-catalog/tooling-and-scripts/spec-folder-literal-naming-ai-derived-slugs.md) |\n   242\t| PHASE-006 | Spec-folder literal naming (create.sh fallback) | [PHASE-006](tooling-and-scripts/spec-folder-literal-naming-create-sh-fallback.md) | [spec-folder-literal-naming-create-sh-fallback](../feature-catalog/tooling-and-scripts/spec-folder-literal-naming-create-sh-fallback.md) |\n   243\t| PHASE-009 | Spec-folder literal naming (remediation rule) | [PHASE-009](to","truncated":true}
{"type":"tool_call","callId":"chatcmpl-tool-a8957e0d1fed7d04","tool":"bash","input":{"command":"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Skilled; echo '=== spec README archive entry ==='; nl -ba .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/README.md | sed -n '108,122p'; echo '=== retrieval doc FT ==='; nl -ba .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/retrieval/retrieval-conventions.md | sed -n '78,88p'; echo '=== playbook relocation lines ==='; nl -ba .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/manual-testing-playbook/tooling-and-scripts/spec-packet-relocation.md | sed -n '1,40p'; nl -ba .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/manual-testing-playbook/tooling-and-scripts/spec-packet-relocation.md | sed -n '130,230p'","description":"Read spec README and playbook line ranges"}}
{"type":"tool_result","callId":"chatcmpl-tool-a8957e0d1fed7d04","status":"completed","result":"=== spec README archive entry ===\n   108\t| `upgrade-level.sh` | Adds missing files and sections for higher documentation levels. |\n   109\t| `validate.sh` | Runs the modular validation gate used before completion claims. `resolve_orchestrator()` checks the compiled runtime dist freshness (via `../lib/dist-freshness.cjs`) before trusting it and fails closed with exit `3` when stale: no silent auto-rebuild. A linked `upgrade-baseline.json` is not applied: the validator warns `UPGRADE_BASELINE_LINK` and the findings it would have downgraded stay errors. `--quiet` prints only the result line. `--include-archive` needs `--recursive`, and exits `2` without it. It also validates the packets in the `z_archive/` of the folder given and, for a track root, of each declared sub-track. On a `--strict` run, a Draft packet whose only errors are derived-metadata rules gets one `repair-derived.cjs --apply` and one revalidation, so the run can write files. `SPECKIT_DRAFT_AUTO_REPAIR=0` (or a set `CI`, or a `SPECKIT_RULES` subset) turns that off. |\n   110\t| `check-completion.sh` | Confirms the `tasks.md` checklist evidence and, when present, acceptance-criteria closure before a task is called complete; the completion sentinel reads its JSON. |\n   111\t| `scaffold-debug-delegation.sh` | Generates `debug-delegation.md` handoff scaffolds from failure-trail input. |\n   112\t| `progressive-validate.sh` | Runs a staged validation pass for detect, fix, suggest and report flows. |\n   113\t| `test-validation.sh` | Legacy wrapper forwarding to `runtime/cli/tests/test-validation.sh`. |\n   114\t| `archive.sh` | Moves completed or stale spec folders into the `z_archive/` beside them: `specs/z_archive/` for a packet at the specs root, `specs/<track>/z_archive/` for a packet in a track, the sub-track's own `z_archive/` for a packet in a sub-track and the parent's own `z_archive/` for a phase. `--restore` returns a folder to the place its archive belongs to. When a live packet with another name already holds its number, the restore lands on the next free number above every live and archived packet there, through `relocate.mjs --from <archived> --to <next> --apply`. `--list` shows every archive's entries by the path that restores them. Archives are found beside the specs root, each track, each declared sub-track and the numbered folders beneath them, without following links, so a copy of a specs tree kept in a packet's research is left out. After every move it runs `repair-derived.cjs` over the moved folder, so the packet and each packet inside it record their new path, and in a track it runs `refresh-track-roots.mjs` for that track, so the track root's `children_ids` follows the packet. After an archive or a plain restore it also asks `ensureDescriptionCache` to rebuild the description cache `specs/descriptions.json` when that file exists, so the cache drops the row for the folder that is gone. A failed rebuild warns and leaves the move in place. A phase parent's `graph-metadata.json` is left as it is, because its writer drops a child only through a reviewed prune. A `z_archive/` that is a symlink is refused on archive and on restore, and `--list` leaves a linked archive out without naming it. An archive or restore path with a `.` or `..` segment is refused before anything resolves it. |\n   115\t| `is-phase-parent.ts` | Detects whether a folder is a phase parent and reports child-count manifest health. |\n   116\t| `sync-phase-map-status.ts` | Corrects a phase parent's map table rows that disagree with their child's status, warns about a blank line that cuts the table short and about children with no row, and reports descendant `completion_pct` mismatches without writing them, since readers take completion from the implementation summary. |\n   117\t| `sweep-track-roots.mjs` | Sweeps every track root (spec-less directory under `specs/` carrying a `graph-metadata.json`) and compares its declared `children_ids` with the numbered child directories that hold a `spec.md`, one line per track; exits 1 when any track differs or holds numbered packets beside declared sub-tracks. A track matches only when the two sets are equal and no packet is declared more than once: equal counts are not enough, since a renamed packet leaves both counts where they were, and a repeated entry leaves the sets equal. A repeat prints `declared more than once: <names>`. In the working tree, a numbered folder without `spec.md` beside sub-tracks prints `numbered folder without spec.md beside sub-tracks` as an advisory diagnostic. Also in the working tree only, a declared sub-track without a `z_archive/` prints `sub-track has no z_archive/; seed it with refresh-track-roots.mjs --apply`, an advisory diagnostic that never changes the exit code. `--rev <commit>` reads that commit instead of the working tree and leaves out symlinked tracks; the pre-push track-root gate runs it that way. Per-packet validation never reaches a track root, because the orchestrator exempts track directories from packet rules. Read-only. |\n   118\t| `refresh-track-roots.mjs` | Rewrites a track root's `children_ids` to its numbered child directories that hold a `spec.md`, dropping entries for packets no longer on disk, repeated entries and entries under an earlier identity. Only `children_ids` changes, and a matching track is not rewritten. Dry run by default (exits 1 when changes are pending); `--apply` writes, and `--track <name>` limits it to one track. Unreadable metadata is reported and left alone, with exit 2. `--apply` also seeds a missing `z_archive/.gitkeep` in each declared sub-track it visits, when that sub-track has no `z_archive/` at all, and a dry run reports it as pending. A linked `z_archive` is refused with `z_archive is a symlink, not written` and exit 2. |\n   119\t| `repair-derived.cjs` | Repairs derivable packet facts (folder name, packet pointer, level, metadata fingerprint) and refuses authored ones; see `README-repair-derived.md`. A linked rewrite target (`description.json`, `graph-metadata.json` or one of the packet documents) is refused: the run prints `left unchanged <file>: symbolic link, not followed` and writes through no link. A linked `graph-metadata.json` is also never re-derived, so the dry run and `--apply` report the same work. Every `UNREADABLE` line names its reason. |\n   120\t| `relocate.mjs` | Moves, renumbers or re-parents spec packets from `--map <file.json>`, `--from` with `--to`, or `--renumber <folder>`, and leaves every store that records a packet path agreeing with the new place. Preflight refuses a destination collision, a taken number (archived siblings count), a track left mixed, a destination deeper than one sub-track, a name that is not `NNN-slug`, a path outside `specs/` or through a link, and uncommitted changes on a path the run would move or rewrite, all before the first write. It then moves each folder (`git mv` when tracked), drops and adds phase-parent `children_ids` for the ids the map names, rewrites every whole old id under `specs/` and recomputes relative markdown links, and drives `migrate-generated-json --only`, `repair-derived.cjs`, `refresh-track-roots.mjs`, `cite-drift-scan.mjs --rebuild-redirects` and `generate-trigger-index.mjs`. Each applied move is appended to `sk-doc/shared/scripts/relocation-ledger.json`, and the run closes with `sweep-track-roots.mjs` and `validate.sh --strict` on each moved packet. A moved path named in `.skilled/bin/lib/compiled-route-layout.cjs` or `.github/workflows/*` is reported and fails the run, and is never rewritten. `--declare-subtrack <track>/<name>` writes a sub-track's `description.json`, `graph-metadata.json` and `z_archive/.gitkeep`. Dry run by default (exits 1 when work is found); `--apply` writes; exit 2 on a refusal or a failed step, and exit 3 when every step and the close sweep landed and only a moved packet's own validation failed. A rerun after status 3 finds nothing to do; a second `--apply` of an applied map also finds nothing to do, and rerunning a map that stopped part-way finishes it. |\n   121\t| `suggest-subtracks.mjs` | Proposes a regrouping of a track from the words its packets already carry. With `--track <name>` alone, it c","truncated":true}
