{"type":"thinking","text":"Potential findings:\nA. Feature catalog \"Spec packet relocation\" (line 66) is missing exit status 3 and `nothing to do` after status 3; contradicts phase 008 D1. Also feature file line 68 says run that stopped on failed step finished by same map, likely covers resume but not late-step marks; the actual important behavior is status 3. Could be P1.\n\nB. Feature catalog root \"Spec packet relocation\" line 690 also omits exit 3. But maybe root entries high-level. Could add to same finding as affected surface.\n\nC. Changelog line 67 same. Changelog is version 2.13.0.0; package currently 2.13.0.0. If code changed without version bump, docs stale. Should we flag as P1? It's release notes stale; yes.\n\nD. Feature catalog \"Sub-track proposal\" line 30 missing non-NNN slug refusal; folder-structure line 141 says exactly three no-map cases. Could be one finding across two docs.\n\nE. Feature catalog archive search line 28 fails to mention `archivedPaths` and claims report shape unchanged; retrieval-conventions line 84 also says only structured/count rows. Could be P1 with cross-surface. The completion criterion requires path JSON marks archived paths. If docs don't mention, consumers miss it. Note code adds archivedPaths unconditionally (even without flag). The docs say without flag none of \"these fields\" appear; an empty archivedPaths appears. That's an exact contradiction. P1 maybe.\n\nF. Restore docs line 145 / spec README 114 omit mixed-track refusal. Maybe not severe? It is a behavior not documented in feature catalog and command README; user may not know restore can fail. P1 traceability? Maybe P2.\n\nG. Feature catalog relocation line 44 says old id matched whole path and longer id left alone; phase 007 added bare name rewrite. It omits saying bare names in phase parents rewritten, so documentation incomplete. P1? Could be P2 unless user can be misled. Also `--renumber` parent spec doc requirement. This is core to completion criterion 5 (after renumber, rg old folder name prints nothing). If docs don't say bare names are rewritten, an operator could hand-edit. But not necessarily severe.\n\nH. Feature catalog relocation line 91 lists only relocate.vitest.ts; phase 010's suite missing. P2.\nI. Feature catalog root line 690 says \"exits 1 when dry run finds work\" only, omits exit 3. P2 maybe.\n\nJ. SKILL.md line 287 says `suggest-subtracks.mjs` names best-fitting sub-track for a description, but does not say command path or that it only works on grouped tracks. It might be fine.\nK. SKILL.md line 295 \"Next spec number\" uses `ls -d specs/[0-9]*/` not archived. That's stale vs D4 (\"Next-number allocation counts archived packets\")! This is a great finding. It tells users to compute next number from live packets only, ignoring `z_archive`, directly contradicting D4 and `create.sh` behavior. P1 correctness/traceability. Cite SKILL.md:295 and feature? This is exactly high-yield.\nL. Root README maybe no \"next number\" command, but may be fine.\nM. `.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/README.md` line 245 says \"It numbers its own packets from 001, keeps its own z_archive\" but maybe doesn't mention numbering counts archived. Line 243 says track archives. Need find \"next number\" in README."}
