{"type":"tool_result","callId":"chatcmpl-tool-a1713a3406a39bc6","status":"completed","result":"=== next number docs ===\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/SKILL.md:295:| Next spec number | `ls -d specs/[0-9]*/ \\| sed 's/.*\\/\\([0-9]*\\)-.*/\\1/' \\| sort -n \\| tail -1` |\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/templates/template-style-guide.md:267:| Section numbering | Sequential, UPPERCASE |\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/templates/template-guide.md:46:3. **Preserve structure** - Preserve section structure and numbering; emojis are optional\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/templates/template-guide.md:278:- Keep numbering sequential (1, 2, 3, ...)\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/templates/template-guide.md:748:2. **Preserve numbering and emojis** - Maintain visual scanning pattern\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/templates/template-guide.md:864:**Why wrong:** Breaks structure, loses numbering, unclear if section was forgotten or intentionally skipped\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/structure/phase-definitions.md:82:1. Create the parent with the explicit track and slug. Replace each angle-bracket value with the actual track, slug, description or packet path before running the commands. `--track <track>` places it under `specs/<track>/`, and the command picks the next number after the highest numbered packet in that track. The result is `specs/<track>/<NNN>-<parent-slug>`. The `phase-parent` level creates one validation child, and there is no `create.sh` mode that skips it. Remove that generated child before moving the existing packet.\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/structure/folder-structure.md:105:│   ├── 001-<slug>/                # numbering restarts inside the sub-track\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/structure/folder-structure.md:421:│   ├── 001-numbering/\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/validation/template-compliance-contract.md:72:- **Section numbering is cosmetic** — the checker strips a leading `N. ` before matching, so renumbering headers never fixes (or breaks) order; only the relative sequence matters.\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/validation/template-compliance-contract.md:154:OPEN QUESTIONS numbering varies by level:\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/feature-catalog/tooling-and-scripts/spec-lifecycle-automation.md:57:| `.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/create.sh` | Script | Creates new spec folders, versioned subfolders, phased parent-child structures, optional git branches, and post-create validation runs. Counts archived numbers when numbering and prints the sub-track advisory line |\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/feature-catalog/tooling-and-scripts/spec-lifecycle-automation.md:70:| `.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/tests/archive-numbering.vitest.ts` | Vitest | Covers `create.sh` numbering after archived packets at the specs root, in a track and in a declared sub-track |\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/feature-catalog/tooling-and-scripts/spec-lifecycle-automation.md:71:| `.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/tests/create-root-numbering.vitest.ts` | Vitest | Covers numbering at the specs root, including after an archived packet |\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/feature-catalog/feature-catalog.md:674:`create.sh`, `recommend-level.sh`, `upgrade-level.sh`, `calculate-completeness.sh`, `check-completion.sh` and `archive.sh` are the entry points. `create.sh` counts archived numbers when it numbers a packet and, with `--track`, prints at most one advisory sub-track line from `suggest-subtracks.mjs`. `archive.sh` archives into the `z_archive/` beside the packet, a declared sub-track's own included, refreshes the description cache after a move and restores a packet whose number is taken onto the next free number through `relocate.mjs`.\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/manual-testing-playbook/tooling-and-scripts/sub-track-proposal.md:65:   printf '{\"level\":\"task\",\"specFolder\":\"tools/003-archive-restore\",\"keywords\":[\"archive restore\",\"restore numbering\"]}\\n' > \"$SUBTRACK_DEMO/specs/tools/003-archive-restore/description.json\"\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/manual-testing-playbook/tooling-and-scripts/sub-track-proposal.md:87:   node .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/suggest-subtracks.mjs --track tools --specs \"$SUBTRACK_DEMO/specs\" --describe \"archive restore numbering\"\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/manual-testing-playbook/tooling-and-scripts/sk-git-worktree-convention.md:3:description: \"This scenario validates the sk-git numbered-worktree convention for `EX-041`. It focuses on creating a wt/{NNNN}-{name} branch in a .worktrees/{NNNN}-{name} directory and confirming the 4-digit global max+1 numbering rule.\"\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/manual-testing-playbook/tooling-and-scripts/sk-git-worktree-convention.md:16:This convention is distinct from the launch wrapper's ephemeral per-session worktrees (`work/{runtime}/{slug}` plus `.worktrees/{runtime}-{slug}`), which are auto-managed, auto-reaped, and intentionally not numbered. The user-observable value is consistent, collision-free workspace isolation: every operator's feature worktrees follow one predictable numbering and directory layout.\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/manual-testing-playbook/tooling-and-scripts/sk-git-worktree-convention.md:24:- Objective: Verify the `wt/{NNNN}-{name}` branch / `.worktrees/{NNNN}-{name}` directory convention and the 4-digit max+1 numbering.\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/manual-testing-playbook/tooling-and-scripts/sk-git-worktree-convention.md:30:- Pass/fail: PASS if the branch name, directory layout, and numbering all follow the sk-git convention.\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/manual-testing-playbook/tooling-and-scripts/sk-git-worktree-convention.md:39:As a tooling validation operator, validate the sk-git worktree numbering against the existing .worktrees/ directory. Compute the next 4-digit counter as max(existing NNNN under .worktrees/) + 1 (or 0001 if none exist) and confirm it is zero-padded to four digits. Return a concise pass/fail verdict with the main reason and cited evidence.\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/manual-testing-playbook/tooling-and-scripts/spec-packet-relocation.md:2:title: \"492 -- Spec packet relocation and renumbering\"\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/manual-testing-playbook/tooling-and-scripts/spec-packet-relocation.md:3:description: \"This scenario validates spec packet relocation for `492`. It focuses on the relocate.mjs dry run, a refused move onto an archived number and an applied renumber, all inside a throwaway copy of the checkout.\"\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/manual-testing-playbook/tooling-and-scripts/spec-packet-relocation.md:7:# 492 -- Spec packet relocation and renumbering\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/manual-testing-playbook/tooling-and-scripts/spec-packet-relocation.md:15:This scenario validates spec packet relocation for `492`. It focuses on the `relocate.mjs` dry run, a refused move onto an archived number and an applied renumber. Every command runs inside a throwaway copy of the checkout under the operating-system temp directory. It never moves or rewrites anything in this checkout's `specs/` tree.\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/manual-testing-playbook/tooling-and-scripts/spec-packet-relocation.md:29:- Prompt: `Renumber the demo track with relocate.mjs in a throwaway copy of this checkout. Show the dry run first, confirm a move onto the archived number 002 is refused, then apply the renumber and report where each packet landed. Return PASS or FAIL with the copy path and the exit codes.`\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/manual-testing-playbook/tooling-and-scripts/spec-packet-relocation.md:42:Renumber the demo track with relocate.mjs in a throwaway copy of this checkout. Show the dry run first, confirm a move onto the archived number 002 is refused, then apply the renumber and report where each packet landed. Return PASS or FAIL with the copy path and the exit codes.\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/manual-testing-playbook/plugins-and-hooks/session-relaunch-claude.md:886:#### HS-5 The live session name is carried across a hop with the next number (Automatable)\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/manual-testing-playbook/plugins-and-hooks/","truncated":true}
