{"type":"tool_result","callId":"chatcmpl-tool-b08c5d18d1a91ab4","status":"completed","result":"=== suggest non-slug test ===\n   200\t    const preflight = spawnSync(process.execPath, [RELOCATE, '--map', mapFile], {\n   201\t      cwd: root,\n   202\t      encoding: 'utf8',\n   203\t    });\n   204\t    expect(preflight.status, preflight.stderr).toBe(1);\n   205\t  });\n   206\t\n   207\t  it('names a packet that cannot be renamed to NNN-slug and prints no map', () => {\n   208\t    const folders = [\n   209\t      '001-alpha-one',\n   210\t      '002-alpha-two',\n   211\t      '003_under',\n   212\t      '004-alpha-four',\n   213\t      '005-beta-one',\n   214\t      '006-beta-two',\n   215\t      '007-beta-three',\n   216\t      '008-beta-four',\n   217\t    ];\n   218\t    const trackDir = writeTrack('demo', folders);\n   219\t    folders.forEach((folder, index) => {\n   220\t      writePacket(trackDir, folder, index < 4 ? ['render', 'window'] : ['cache', 'store']);\n   221\t    });\n   222\t\n   223\t    const result = run('--track', 'demo');\n   224\t    expect(result.status, result.stderr).toBe(0);\n   225\t    expect(result.stdout).toMatch(/003_under[^\\n]*must be renamed first/);\n   226\t    expect(result.stdout).toContain('no map');\n   227\t    expect(result.stdout).not.toContain('\"from\"');\n   228\t  });\n   229\t\n   230\t  it('withholds a map below the threshold and prints one when the threshold drops', () => {\n   231\t    buildSmallDemo();\n   232\t    const held = run('--track', 'demo');\n=== code non-slug ===\n   286\t    group.name = name;\n   287\t    used.add(name);\n   288\t  }\n   289\t}\n   290\t\n   291\tfunction proposeRetroactive(specsRoot, track, layout, threshold) {\n   292\t  const folders = [...layout.packets].sort(compareNames);\n   293\t  const misnamed = folders.filter((folder) => !MAP_PACKET_NAME.test(folder));\n   294\t  if (misnamed.length > 0) {\n   295\t    for (const folder of misnamed) {\n   296\t      process.stdout.write(`track ${track}: packet ${folder} is not NNN-slug and must be renamed first\\n`);\n   297\t    }\n   298\t    process.stdout.write(`track ${track}: no map\\n`);\n   299\t    return;\n   300\t  }\n   301\t\n   302\t  if (layout.subTracks.length > 0) {\n   303\t    process.stdout.write(`track ${track} is already grouped into sub-tracks; no map\\n`);\n   304\t    return;\n   305\t  }\n   306\t\n   307\t  if (folders.length < threshold) {\n   308\t    process.stdout.write(`track ${track} has ${folders.length} live packets, below the threshold of ${threshold}; no map\\n`);\n   309\t    return;\n   310\t  }\n   311\t\n   312\t  const termsByFolder = new Map();\n=== folder-structure 135-143 ===\n   135\t**When a flat track has grown.** A flat track with 8 or more live packets is a candidate. `--threshold <n>` changes that number. The tool clusters the track's packets by the terms their `description.json` and `graph-metadata.json` share and prints a whole-track map:\n   136\t\n   137\t```bash\n   138\tnode .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/suggest-subtracks.mjs --track <track> > map.json\n   139\t```\n   140\t\n   141\tFor a flat track, the map names every live packet of the track exactly once, because a track holds either packets or sub-tracks and never both. The tool prints no map in three cases, each with one line and exit `0`: a track below the threshold, a track where no grouping is found, and a track that already has a declared sub-track.\n   142\t\n   143\tA track that already has a declared sub-track gets `track <track> is already grouped into sub-tracks; no map`, also when numbered packets still sit beside the sub-tracks. For such a track, ask where each packet fits with `--describe`, which prints `best fit: <track>/<sub-track>` or `none fits: propose a new sub-track in <track>`. Then write the map by hand, one `{ \"from\": \"<track>/NNN-slug\", \"to\": \"<track>/<sub-track>/NNN-slug\" }` entry for every packet still at the track level, and run it through `relocate.mjs --map`. The map must cover all of them, because `relocate.mjs` refuses a plan that leaves flat packets beside sub-tracks. A single remaining packet can move with `relocate.mjs --from <path> --to <path>`.\n   144\t\n"}
