{"type":"tool_result","callId":"chatcmpl-tool-bc04bc441394cdb4","status":"completed","result":"817:It keeps a vendored copy's own changes. `/doctor:overlay` reports an overlay that drifted and restores it, and it re-pins the copy to a newer upstream commit. It can also audit drift no overlay owns, move a source kept off its layout path, and take over a lock a run that has ended left behind. See [Copy It Into Your Project](INSTALL-SKILLED.md#4-copy-it-into-your-project). The other six doctor commands stay with the skill whose own checks they run, such as `/doctor:git` with `sk-git`. The [Doctor](#doctor) section lists them.\n1310:| `/doctor:agents-md` | `check`, `embed`, `restore` | `check` | `embed`, `restore` |\n1342:- `rebuild` rebuilds `skill-graph.sqlite` from the checked-in `graph-metadata.json` files through the advisor CLI, after a backup it restores when the rebuild fails\n1398:- `repin --rollback <run-id>` restores that backup after its own yes\n1402:**`/doctor:agents-md [check|embed|restore] [--json] [--root <dir>] [--dry-run] [--plan-digest <digest>] [--run <dir>] [--yes]`** - your root `AGENTS.md` against the shipped template\n1405:- `embed` composes in memory and shows every target with its diff, the new block, the byte budget and the lines it will keep. Then it prints a plan digest. It writes only when you give that digest back and backs up every path it touches first. Afterwards it proves that not one of your lines was dropped, and restores from the backup itself when one is\n1406:- `restore` restores exactly the paths one recorded run wrote, and removes the files, and the empty folders, that run created\n243:The track folder itself, `specs/<track>/`, holds no spec docs. Its `graph-metadata.json` lists the track's packets in `children_ids`. `create.sh --track` adds each new packet to that list, `archive.sh` refreshes it after moving a packet into the track's own `z_archive/` or back, `refresh-track-roots.mjs --apply` rewrites it from the packet folders on disk, and the pre-push hook blocks a pushed commit whose list disagrees with the packets it holds.\n638:| `archive.sh` | archive completed spec folders into the `z_archive/` beside them, which for a packet in a declared sub-track is the sub-track's own `z_archive/`. `--restore` returns a folder to the place its archive belongs to, and when a live packet already holds its number it lands on the next free number, counting archived packets, through `relocate.mjs`. After an archive or a plain restore the description cache `specs/descriptions.json` is rebuilt when it exists |\n288:| Track-root lists | `node .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/refresh-track-roots.mjs --apply` after moving, renaming or deleting a packet in a track by hand; `archive.sh` refreshes it itself. The pre-push hook blocks a commit whose track lists other packets than it holds |\n"}
