{"type":"thinking","text":"Need maybe inspect all docs for exact findings and route. Let's identify iteration 1 correctness findings. We need cite exact file:line and verified code. Let's make 2-3 P1s:\nF1: Feature catalog relocation contradicts exit status contract by listing only 0/1/2 and treating status 3 as failed close. Evidence: feature doc line 66; code line 1661; phase 008 goal D1. Also root README line 416 and skill README line 639 omit exit statuses. But primary line 66. Impact: consumers treat status 3 as failed run and repeat/abort; temp copy tests expected to exit 0 on rerun. This is correctness/traceability. P1.\n\nF2: `SKILL.md` next spec number command ignores archived packets, contrary D4. Evidence: SKILL.md:295; create.sh:1644; phase 008 D4. P1.\n\nF3: `phase-definitions.md` says next number after highest numbered packet in track, omitting archived. Evidence line 82; create.sh 1644 includes z_archive. P2? This is same class as F2, maybe group as cross-consumer finding (one finding with multiple refs). The review doctrine says finding schema; one finding can have multiple locations, but `file` primary. To avoid duplication, group F2/F3 into one cross-consumer finding: \"Next-number guidance ignores archived packets in two published surfaces.\" That's good.\n\nF4: `feature-catalog/spec-packet-relocation` line 68 says \"run that stopped on a failed step is finished by running same map again\" but phase 006 introduced late-step ledger marks; if the run stopped on the close sweep or validation, the rerun now repeats the close and status 3. Does line 68 conflict? It says \"failed step\" generic. Maybe not. The more important missing is exit 3. Could also mention no description of late-step ledger marks, so docs understate how resume works. But not a contradiction except exit 3. One finding.\n\nF5: `spec/README` line 120 is updated and can be cited as correct baseline. Good.\n\nF6: `README.md` line 416 lacks exit codes but high-level. Maybe P2 not P1.\n\nF7: `SKILL.md` line 295 is a command that simply computes live max; no archived. Should definitely be P1 because it gives an exact wrong command.\n\nF8: docs `feature-catalog/feature-catalog.md` line 690 says dry run exits 1, no status 3; could be part of F1.\n\nF9: `changelog/v2.13.0.0.md` line 67 says only 0/1/2 and \"map stopped part-way finishes\". Could be part of F1 with affected surfaces. This is high-value.\n\nF10: `manual-testing-playbook` scenario lacks exit 3 and resume. Could be P2 in later iteration.\n\nCould F1 be P1: Yes.\n\nCould F2 be P1: Yes.\n\nMaybe F3: `folder-structure.md` line 141 missing non-slug refusal. That's correctness. We can save for iteration 3.\n\nIteration 1 dimension correctness, focus docs vs code. We can report 2 P1 and maybe 1 P2:\n- P2: `feature-catalog/spec-packet-relocation.md` line 60 says \"two entries\" but not two case-folded spellings; code handles case-folded duplicates. Does this matter? It's an omitted refusal. P2 docs completeness.\n- P2: `README.md` line 416 / skill README line 639 don't mention status 3. But docs are high-level and may not need. Could be P2.\nMaybe 2 P1 and 1 P2 is enough.\n\nNeed ensure no duplicate findings in subsequent iterations. We'll use unique IDs R1-P1-001, R1-P1-002, R1-P2-003. The records' findingDetails must have id/severity/title.\n\nNeed delta rows: iteration record first, then finding rows, classification, traceability checks, ruled_out. We need ensure reducer picks findings from delta. It may use delta records. We'll include `{\"type\":\"finding\",\"id\":\"R1-P1-001\",\"severity\":\"P1\",\"title\":\"...\",\"file\":\"...:66\",\"iteration\":1,...}`. Need fields maybe `findingId` expected? `deltaRecordToFinding` likely accepts `id` or `findingId`. Prompt says use id. Good. It may need cluster? We'll include.\n\nNeed narrative structure. The skill's template says sections: Dispatcher, Files Reviewed, Findings - New (with P0/P1/P2), Traceability Checks, Integration Evidence, Edge Cases, Confirmed-Clean Surfaces, Ruled Out, Next Focus. But parser expects `Findings` and subsections. We'll use:\n# Iteration 1 - Correctness ...\n## Dispatcher\n## Files Reviewed\n## Findings - New\n### P0 Findings\nNone.\n### P1 Findings\n1. **Title** -- file:line -- ...\nCase: ...\nFinding class: ...\nScope proof: ...\nAffected surface hints: ...\nClaim adjudication: ```json ...```\n### P2 Findings\n...\n## Traceability Checks\n### Core\n...\n### Overlay\n...\n## Integration Evidence\n...\n## Edge Cases\n...\n## Confirmed-Clean Surfaces\n...\n## Ruled Out\n...\n## Next Focus\n...\n## Assessment\nDimensions addressed: correctness\n\nBut parser `extractSubsection(findingsSection, 'P1')` might match. Fine. It extracts findings; no impact on reducer since we provide findingDetails. The final line must be exactly \"Review verdict: CONDITIONAL\" since P1s. Good.\n\nNeed write strategy update after iteration. The persona says update strategy manually. But the reducer also updates machine sections. We can update specific sections: mark correctness [x] in section 3? The reducer will replace section 3 with remaining dimensions based on coverage. It will mark correctness checked if record dimensions includes correctness. So we can leave and let reducer. But the guideline says update strategy before gateway; the reducer runs after gateway and updates. We can manually update WHAT WORKED/WHAT FAILED and edge cases, next focus. Then reducer updates machine sections. That satisfies. We should use edit tool, not write whole file. For each iteration, edit strategy sections. Good.\n\nNeed gateway record after iteration file and strategy coherent. Then reducer. Then delta? The prompt says create delta after gateway. The reducer consumes delta, but if we run reducer before delta it won't see findings. Wait workflow order: dispatch, evaluate, claim adjudication, reduce state, graph upsert, dashboard, update tracking. The delta is written by the agent BEFORE dispatch returns, so reducer sees it. The agent step says write findings, update strategy, record state, write delta, verify outputs. Actually step order in persona: 7 write findings, 8 update strategy, 9 record state, 10 write delta, 11 verify. The workflow then reducer. So we must create delta file before running reducer. It includes iteration record and finding rows. The gateway record file is separate. We can write delta after gateway, before reducer. Good.\n\nNeed append gateway only iteration record. Then reducer with artifact dir. It will read state log (iteration record) and delta and iteration file. It may also ingest findingDetails from record. Good.\n\nNeed compute `newFindingsRatio`: weightedNew/weightedTotal. For iteration 1, all findings new and no prior. If 2 P1 (10) + 1 P2 (1) = 21, new=21, total=21 => 1.0. If any refinement, no. Set 1.0.\n\nNeed durationMs approximate. Use timestamp. The tool reads clock; we can use current date. We'll use node to generate timestamp or `date`. The record must include `timestamp` ISO now and `durationMs`. Fine.\n\nNeed record `findingsNew`: prompt says array of new-finding entries, but reducer allows severity object. The workflow error row uses object; template says array. We can use array of finding IDs? The prompt says findingsNew list? The skill says required field. The example uses []. The reducer may expect array or object. To be safe, use array of finding detail objects or IDs. Let's inspect reducer's treatment of findingsNew."}
