{"type":"tool_result","callId":"chatcmpl-tool-a598dfc8f6500cb8","status":"completed","result":"44:| D1 | `relocate.mjs` gains one exit status, 3, for a run whose steps and sweep all passed and whose only failure is a moved packet's validation. Statuses 0, 1 and 2 keep their meaning otherwise. A run that ends on 3 has landed, so the same call again prints `relocate: nothing to do` and exits 0. This amends decision D1 of phase 006 for that one case, and REQ-001 and REQ-012 of phase 001, as the parent `spec.md` Operator Decisions record. |\n47:| D4 | A new phase is numbered above every live and archived phase of its parent, and its predecessor is the highest live phase. |\n44:| D1 | The exit status of `relocate.mjs` keeps its three meanings: 0 nothing left to do, 1 work found on a dry run, 2 a refusal or a failed step. Phase 008 amends this for one case of the close. |\n46:| D3 | A finished map still ends on `relocate: nothing to do` with exit 0. |\n120:| `relocate.mjs` | Moves, renumbers or re-parents spec packets from `--map <file.json>`, `--from` with `--to`, or `--renumber <folder>`, and leaves every store that records a packet path agreeing with the new place. Preflight refuses a destination collision, a taken number (archived siblings count), a track left mixed, a destination deeper than one sub-track, a name that is not `NNN-slug`, a path outside `specs/` or through a link, and uncommitted changes on a path the run would move or rewrite, all before the first write. It then moves each folder (`git mv` when tracked), drops and adds phase-parent `children_ids` for the ids the map names, rewrites every whole old id under `specs/` and recomputes relative markdown links, and drives `migrate-generated-json --only`, `repair-derived.cjs`, `refresh-track-roots.mjs`, `cite-drift-scan.mjs --rebuild-redirects` and `generate-trigger-index.mjs`. Each applied move is appended to `sk-doc/shared/scripts/relocation-ledger.json`, and the run closes with `sweep-track-roots.mjs` and `validate.sh --strict` on each moved packet. A moved path named in `.skilled/bin/lib/compiled-route-layout.cjs` or `.github/workflows/*` is reported and fails the run, and is never rewritten. `--declare-subtrack <track>/<name>` writes a sub-track's `description.json`, `graph-metadata.json` and `z_archive/.gitkeep`. Dry run by default (exits 1 when work is found); `--apply` writes; exit 2 on a refusal or a failed step, and exit 3 when every step and the close sweep landed and only a moved packet's own validation failed. A rerun after status 3 finds nothing to do; a second `--apply` of an applied map also finds nothing to do, and rerunning a map that stopped part-way finishes it. |\n82:1. Create the parent with the explicit track and slug. Replace each angle-bracket value with the actual track, slug, description or packet path before running the commands. `--track <track>` places it under `specs/<track>/`, and the command picks the next number after the highest numbered packet in that track. The result is `specs/<track>/<NNN>-<parent-slug>`. The `phase-parent` level creates one validation child, and there is no `create.sh` mode that skips it. Remove that generated child before moving the existing packet.\n295:| Next spec number | `ls -d specs/[0-9]*/ \\| sed 's/.*\\/\\([0-9]*\\)-.*/\\1/' \\| sort -n \\| tail -1` |\n"}
