{"type":"tool_result","callId":"chatcmpl-tool-8f3d29f8cae6f9e6","status":"completed","result":"66:Exit status 0 means nothing is left to do, and after `--apply` it means every step landed and the close passed. Status 1 means a dry run found work. Status 2 means a rejected argument, a refused plan, a failed step or a failed close.\n68:The run is safe to repeat. An entry whose folder already sits at its destination is checked for stale records only, a second `--apply` of an applied map finds nothing to do, and a run that stopped on a failed step is finished by running the same map again.\n67:Exit 0 means nothing is left to do. Exit 1 means a dry run found work. Exit 2 means the plan was refused or a step failed. A second `--apply` of the same map prints `relocate: nothing to do`. A map that stopped part-way finishes on the next run.\n690:`relocate.mjs` takes one mode: `--map`, `--from` with `--to`, `--renumber` or `--declare-subtrack`. It prints the plan and exits 1 when a dry run finds work, and `--apply` writes. Every refusal happens before the first write. An applied run moves the folders, rewrites references under `specs/`, re-derives the packets' recorded paths, refreshes the track roots, the relocation ledger, the redirect table and the trigger index, then closes with the track-root sweep and strict validation of each moved packet. Code and CI files are never rewritten: a moved path named there refuses the run.\n"}
