{"type":"tool_result","callId":"chatcmpl-tool-88e568faf0d3eb14","status":"completed","result":"=== search.md ===\n3:argument-hint: \"<query> [--packet <specFolder>] [--triggers] [--paths] [--count] [--include-archive]\"\n88:3. Render candidates with the Section 2 contract in the presentation asset — score, match class and path, in the order the tool returned them.\n98:| Which files mention it (`--paths`) | Section 2.2 | `--files-with-matches` |\n108:Narrow with one `--search-root <path>` per root in place of the default `specs .skilled`. Pass `--limit <n>` when the user asks for more files, and `--limit 0` for all of them. The record's `command` field is the exact `rg` line that ran. The wrapper reads a phrase that starts with `--` as a flag and exits `2`; run the raw Section 2.1 recipe for that phrase instead. The other three modes run their recipe directly.\n110:Archived packets are left out by default. Add `--include-archive` to any wrapper recipe to search them as well:\n113:node .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/retrieval/rg-wrapper.mjs path 'skill routing refactor' --include-archive\n116:A phrase that only an archived packet holds exits `1` without the flag and `0` with it, and each archived path ends `[archived]`. The flag drops the `!**/z_archive/**` glob from the recipe and marks every printed hit under a `z_archive` segment with `[archived]`. The JSON rows of the structured and count recipes carry `archived: true|false`. A second invocation then lists the `description.json` and `graph-metadata.json` files of archived packets that hold the phrase, under a `json    :` section, and the exit is `0` when either lane matches. The mode is opt-in only. `/speckit:resume` excludes archives and has no such flag, and the trigger-index lane never reads them.\n118:1. Resolve the search roots. Narrow by path, never by pattern: `specs .skilled` for everything, `specs/<track>` for one track, `specs/<track>/<sub-track>` for one declared sub-track, `specs/<track>/<NNN-name>` for one packet, `specs/<track>/<sub-track>/<NNN-name>` for a packet inside a sub-track, `specs/<track>/<NNN-name>/<NNN-child-name>` for one phase child. `--packet <specFolder>` replaces the roots with that path.\n119:2. Run exactly one recipe. Never combine `--json` with the path-only or count mode: ripgrep does not reject the combination, the last output-mode flag wins silently, and a JSONL parser handed count output sees an empty result rather than an error.\n121:4. Keep the wrapper's `results` in the order it returned them: it already applied the ranking tuple in `retrieval-conventions.md` Section 5 — evidence field, then normalized match class, then relative path and one-based line. Order raw-recipe output with the same tuple. Ripgrep supplies matches, paths and lines; it never ranks relevance, and no rendered output may imply that it does.\n=== search presentation ===\n# SpecKit Search Presentation Contract\n\nSingle source of truth for `/speckit:search` startup questions and result displays.\n\nRegister (COSTAR): these contracts are written objective-first for an automated-pipeline audience — fixed response shapes, no preamble, no conversational framing inside the rendered block. This is the wording style of the contract itself, not a prompt framework imposed on callers.\n\n## Template Index\n\nStart with the matching render contract before drafting any response:\n\n- Trigger-index results: Section 2, `SPECKIT:SEARCH TRIGGERS \"<query>\" ... STATUS=OK CANDIDATES=<count>`.\n- Free-text evidence results: Section 3, `SPECKIT:SEARCH \"<query>\" ... STATUS=OK RESULTS=<count>`.\n- No-hit results: Section 4, the clean empty result.\n- Unsupported requests: Section 6.\n- Errors: Section 7.\n\n## 1. Startup Question Policy\n\nThis section applies ONLY when the command's `ARGUMENT RESOLUTION` header reported `ARGS_PRESENT=false`. If `ARGS_PRESENT=true`, skip this section entirely and render the result for the resolved `QUERY` — never ask the startup question over a populated query.\n\nWhen `ARGS_PRESENT=false` (bare invocation), ask one open-ended question:\n\n```text\nWhat phrase should I look for?\n```\n\nAccept any natural-language answer as the query. Do not dump a menu at startup.\n\nAsk a targeted follow-up only when genuinely ambiguous:\n\n| Ambiguity | Targeted question |\n| --- | --- |\n| The query is a single generic workflow word (`session`, `context`, `memory`, `summary`) | `That phrase is too generic to be distinctive. What specific term, decision, symbol or failure symptom should I look for?` |\n| The user names a packet but no phrase | `Which phrase should I look for inside that packet?` |\n| The user asks for lineage, drift, ablations or dashboards | Render the unsupported notice in Section 6. |\n\n## 2. Trigger-Index Result Display\n\nThe keyed lane. Renders the output of `lookup-trigger-index.mjs` — a match against author-declared `trigger_phrases`, not a scan of prose.\n\n```text\nSPECKIT:SEARCH TRIGGERS \"<query>\"\n--------------------------------------------------\nindex     <indexHash short>   manifest <manifestHash short>\nscope     <specFolder or (unscoped)>\nfallback   : <files> unindexed doc(s) read, <matches> match(es) (when staleFallback is available)\n<score>  <matchClass>  <path>\n<score>  <matchClass>  <path>\n+<hidden> more candidate(s) not shown (raise --limit to see them)\n\nSTATUS=OK CANDIDATES=<count> LANE=trigger-index\n```\n\nField mapping:\n\n| Source field | Template slot |\n| --- | --- |\n| The resolved `QUERY` | `\"<query>\"` |\n| `indexHash`, `manifestHash` | `index` / `manifest`, first 12 characters each |\n| `specFolder` | `scope`, or `(unscoped)` |\n| `result.score` | `<score>` — the lookup's own score, three decimals, exactly as the tool emits it |\n| `result.matchClass` | `<matchClass>` — one of `exact`, `phrase-containment`, `query-containment`, `token-overlap`, `partial`, verbatim from the tool |\n| `result.path` | `<path>` — the repo-relative document path |\n| `results.length`, the rows shown after `--limit` | `CANDIDATES=<count>` |\n| `totalCandidates` - `results.length`, only when `truncated` is true | `+<hidden> more candidate(s)` line; omit the line when `truncated` is false |\n| `staleFallback` | Render the `fallback   : <files> unindexed doc(s) read, <matches> match(es)` line when `available` is true, adding the cap note when `truncated` is true. Render `fallback   : unavailable (not a git work tree)` when `available` is false. |\n| A `result.path` listed in `staleFallback.paths` | Append `[not yet in index]` to that result's path so fallback matches are identified as unindexed spec docs. |\n\nRules:\n- Render the `+<hidden> more` line only when `truncated` is true, and compute `<hidden>` from the tool's `totalCandidates`, never from a guess.\n- Render the `fallback` line only when `staleFallback` is present. Mark each result path listed in `staleFallback.paths` with `[not yet in index]`.\n- Render candidates in the order the tool returned them. The lookup is deterministic; do not re-sort.\n- Never rename `score` to `confidence`, `similarity` or `relevance`, and never render it as a percentage. It is the tool's own score, not a probability.\n- `matchClass` is a label, not a rank. Do not translate it into a quality adjective.\n\n## 3. Free-Text Evidence Display\n\nThe scan lane. Renders parsed ripgrep output, addressed by path and one-based line.\n\n```text\nSPECKIT:SEARCH \"<query>\"\n--------------------------------------------------\nrecipe    <section id from retrieval-conventions.md>\nroots     <positional search roots>\n<path>:<line>  <field>  <matchClass> (+N more in this file)\n<path>:<line>  <field>  <matchClass> (+N more in this file)  [archived]\njson    : <count> archived metadata file(s) (only with --include-archive)\n<path>  [archived]\n\nSTATUS=OK RESULTS=<shown rows> HIDDEN=<files>/<matches> LANE=ripgrep\n```\n\nFilled example:\n\n```text\nSPECKIT:SEARCH \"trigger index generator\"\n--------------------------------------------------\nrecipe    2.2 path-only\nroots     specs/system-speckit/runtime-and-release/001-system-speckit-v4/017-memory-database-decommission\nspecs/system-speckit/runtime-and-release/001-system-speckit-v4/017-memory-database-decommission/001-trigger-index-replacement/spec.md:14  trigger_phrases  exact\nspecs/system-speckit/runtime-and-release/001-system-speckit-v4/017-memory-da","truncated":true}
