usal.\n- Phase 008 goal D3 at line 46? Let's get.\n- `spec/README.md:114` describes archive.sh; no mixed-track. `feature-catalog/tooling-and-scripts/spec-lifecycle-automation.md:45` describes archive; no mixed-track. `manual-testing-playbook/tooling-and-scripts/spec-lifecycle-automation.md:219-220` notes restore numbering; no mixed-track. `system-spec-kit/README.md:638` no mixed-track. `changelog` line 145 no mixed-track.\n- Maybe `folder-structure.md:143` says `relocate.mjs` refuses a plan that leaves flat packets beside sub-tracks, but not that `archive.sh --restore` also refuses. That's a key gap: docs say only relocation refuses. Great. We can primary `folder-structure.md:143`. The actual code calls relocate preflight and refuses. This is a security/trust-boundary doc gap: restore bypass could create mixed track if not refused. P1.\n- Evidence: `archive.sh:358-395`; `archive-track.vitest.ts:641-690`; phase 008 goal D3 line.\n- Case: track with a declared sub-track and archived flat packet; restore prints refusal and exits 1; docs promise restore returns it to its home and only mentions next-number. A caller sees a failure no doc predicts.\n\nCould be P1. The user focus explicitly says mixed-track restore refusal. Good.\n\nR2-P2-005: Path/symlink refusal documentation inconsistency? Maybe docs in `folder-structure.md` archive section only says z_archive prefix; doesn't mention symlink/path refusal. But `spec/README.md` does. Not necessary. Could skip.\n\nR2-P2-006: `archive.sh` command documentation says \"restore returns a folder to the place its archive belongs to\" and doesn't mention status 3 restore success. But phase 008 D2 says a renumbered restore that ends on status 3 exits 0 and warns. The `archive.sh` help notes? Let's inspect help lines 80-95 maybe no status 3. `spec/README` line 114 no. Feature lifecycle line 45 says if relocate fails, restore exits 1, no status 3 handling. This is another gap. Could combine with mixed-track. But then finding gets broad. Maybe two P1s:\n- mixed-track restore refusal missing.\n- restore status-3 success path missing (renumbered restore exits 0 and warns). Evidence archive.sh:437-440; phase 008 goal D2. Docs say \"if relocate run fails, restore exits 1\" in feature lifecycle line 45, which is false for status 3. That's a direct contradiction! Great. `feature-catalog/tooling-and-scripts/spec-lifecycle-automation.md:45` says \"If `relocate.mjs` is missing or its run fails, the restore exits with status 1...\" but status 3 is a run that \"failed\" validation yet archive treats as success and exits 0. This is a P1 correctness/security doc mismatch. Excellent.\n- Primary `feature-catalog/tooling-and-scripts/spec-lifecycle-automation.md:45`. Code `archive.sh:437-440`. Phase 008 D2 line 45.\n- Also `spec/README.md:114` doesn't mention status 3; but its archive entry says next number through relocate and no mention. Could be P2.\nThis gives security dimension two P1s. Good.\n\nMaybe R2-P2-007: `archive.sh --help` / docs omit restore validation warning. The manual playbook scenario 237 only tests help text. P2 maybe.\n\nLet's get line refs: phase 008 D2/D3 lines."}
