{"type":"tool_result","callId":"chatcmpl-tool-9c85c10c62487115","status":"completed","result":"    50\t\n    51\tshow_help() {\n    52\t    cat << 'EOF'\n    53\tarchive-spec.sh - Archive completed spec folders\n    54\t\n    55\tUSAGE:\n    56\t    archive-spec.sh <spec-folder>\n    57\t    archive-spec.sh --list\n    58\t    archive-spec.sh --restore <archived-folder>\n    59\t\n    60\tOPTIONS:\n    61\t    --list, -l          List all archived specs\n    62\t    --restore, -r       Restore an archived spec folder\n    63\t    --force, -f         Skip completeness check (archive anyway)\n    64\t    --help, -h          Show this help message\n    65\t\n    66\tEXAMPLES:\n    67\t    archive-spec.sh specs/051-feature-name/\n    68\t    archive-spec.sh --force specs/051-feature-name/\n    69\t    archive-spec.sh specs/my-track/012-feature-name/\n    70\t    archive-spec.sh specs/my-track/my-sub/012-feature-name/\n    71\t    archive-spec.sh specs/my-track/012-feature-name/003-phase-name/\n    72\t    archive-spec.sh --list\n    73\t    archive-spec.sh --restore specs/z_archive/051-feature-name/\n    74\t    archive-spec.sh --restore specs/my-track/z_archive/012-feature-name/\n    75\t    archive-spec.sh --restore specs/my-track/012-feature-name/z_archive/003-phase-name/\n    76\t\n    77\tNOTES:\n    78\t    - Specs with <90% completeness will prompt for confirmation\n    79\t    - Use --force to skip the completeness check\n    80\t    - A spec is moved into the z_archive/ beside it: specs/z_archive/ at the\n    81\t      specs root, specs/<track>/z_archive/ in a track, a declared sub-track's\n    82\t      own z_archive/ for its packets, <parent>/z_archive/ for a phase\n    83\t    - Restore returns a spec to the folder its z_archive/ belongs to\n    84\t    - A restore whose number a live packet already holds lands on the next free\n    85\t      number, counting archived packets, through relocate.mjs\n    86\t    - A z_archive/ that is a symlink is refused on archive and on restore\n    87\t    - An archive or restore argument that passes through a symlink is refused,\n    88\t      and the message names the real folder to use instead\n    89\t    - An archive or restore path with a . or .. segment is refused, since a\n    90\t      segment can reach a linked z_archive/ that the literal path does not show\n    91\t    - A track's graph-metadata.json list is refreshed after both moves; a\n    92\t      declared sub-track's list and its track's are refreshed together\n    93\t    - A phase parent's graph-metadata.json is left as it is: its writer drops\n    94\t      a child only through a reviewed prune\n    95\tEOF\n    96\t}\n    97\t\n    98\tlog_info() { echo -e \"${BLUE}INFO:${NC} $1\"; }\n    99\tlog_success() { echo -e \"${GREEN}SUCCESS:${NC} $1\"; }\n   100\tlog_warning() { echo -e \"${YELLOW}WARNING:${NC} $1\"; }\n"}
