le, downgrade to P2.',\n    case: 'A track archive holds 001-old and a live packet holds its number; the restored packet fails strict validation, archive.sh exits 0 with a warning, but the page says a failed relocation exits 1.'\n  },\n  {\n    id: 'R2-P1-005', severity: 'P1', title: 'The archive command reference and lifecycle docs omit the mixed-track restore refusal',\n    file: '.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/README.md:114',\n    findingClass: 'cross-consumer',\n    scopeProof: 'rg for mixed-track and \"would hold flat packets\" over the changed docs returns only relocation-preflight language and tests; none of the archive-facing docs names the restore refusal.',\n    affectedSurfaceHints: ['archive command reference', 'feature catalog lifecycle page', 'changelog restore section', 'skill README command table', 'archive.sh --help'],\n    claim: 'The archive command reference and lifecycle docs do not document the mixed-track restore refusal, although archive.sh asks the relocation preflight and exits 1 when the restore would leave flat packets beside sub-tracks.',\n    evidenceRefs: ['runtime/cli/spec/README.md:114', '008-restore-and-phase-numbering/goal.md:46', 'runtime/cli/spec/archive.sh:363', 'runtime/cli/spec/archive.sh:394', 'runtime/cli/tests/archive-track.vitest.ts:645'],\n    counterevidenceSought: 'Searched the command reference, lifecycle page, changelog, skill README, and archive help for the mixed-track line; only the relocation docs mention mixed-track, and they apply it to a map, not to restore.',\n    alternativeExplanation: 'The guard is new and narrow, but it changes the restore exit contract and adds a recovery command, so omitting it leaves the documented command incomplete.',\n    finalSeverity: 'P1', confidence: 0.94,\n    downgradeTrigger: 'If the archive docs link to the relocation preflight and explicitly say restore can be refused for mixed-track, downgrade to P2.',\n    case: 'A track has a declared sub-track and an archived flat packet; the restore would mix layouts, archive.sh refuses with exit 1, and the command reference predicts a successful restore.'\n  },\n  {\n    id: 'R2-P2-006', severity: 'P2', title: 'archive.sh --help omits both new restore outcomes',\n    file: '.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/archive.sh:83',\n    findingClass: 'instance-only',\n    scopeProof: 'The help heredoc at archive.sh:52-95 is the only command-level help block; no other archive help text exists.',\n    affectedSurfaceHints: ['archive.sh --help', 'archive command reference'],\n    claim: 'The built-in help lists only the happy-path restore and next-number notes; it omits the mixed-track refusal and the status-3 success warning.',\n    evidenceRefs: ['runtime/cli/spec/archive.sh:77', 'runtime/cli/spec/archive.sh:95', 'runtime/cli/spec/archive.sh:363', 'runtime/cli/spec/archive.sh:437'],\n    counterevidenceSought: 'The full help heredoc was read; neither branch appears.',\n    alternativeExplanation: 'The help may intentionally stay terse, but it already enumerates restore edge cases such as symlinks and dot segments.',\n    finalSeverity: 'P2', confidence: 0.9,\n    downgradeTrigger: 'No further downgrade; close as advisory when the help notes name both branches.',\n    case: 'An operator runs archive.sh --help and sees no mixed-track refusal or status-3 warning before a restore.'\n  }\n];\nconst record = {\n  type: 'iteration', iteration: 2, run: 'fanout-dsh-1-1794652127582-mfqldk-i2',\n  mode: 'review', target_agent: 'deep-review', agent_definition_loaded: true,\n  resolved_route: 'Resolved route: mode=review target_agent=deep-review',\n  status: 'complete', focus: 'security: restore trust boundary and mixed-track refusal',\n  dimensions: ['security'],\n  filesReviewed: [\n    'specs/system-speckit/spec-folder-tooling/005-subtrack-proposal-and-archive-reach/008-restore-and-phase-numbering/goal.md:44',\n    '.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/archive.sh:363',\n    '.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/tests/archive-track.vitest.ts:645',\n    '.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/README.md:114',\n    '.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/feature-catalog/tooling-and-scripts/spec-lifecycle-automation.md:45',\n    '.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/manual-testing-playbook/tooling-and-scripts/spec-lifecycle-automation.md:219',\n    '.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/README.md:638',\n    '.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/changelog/v2.13.0.0.md:145'\n  ],\n  findingsCount: findings.length,\n  findingsSummary: { P0: 0, P1: 2, P2: 1 },\n  findingsNew: findings.map((f) => ({ id: f.id, severity: f.severity, title: f.title })),\n  findingDetails: findings,\n  traceabilityChecks: {\n    summary: { required: 6, executed: 5, pass: 0, partial: 4, fail: 1, blocked: 0, notApplicable: 1, gatingFailures: 0 },\n    results: [\n      { protocolId: 'spec_code', level: 'core', status: 'partial', gateClass: 'soft', evidence: 'Restore status 3 and mixed-track refusal are implemented; changed docs state the wrong contract.' },\n      { protocolId: 'checklist_evidence', level: 'core', status: 'partial', gateClass: 'soft', evidence: 'Phase 008 criteria include both restore branches; lifecycle docs omit both.' },\n      { protocolId: 'skill_agent', level: 'overlay', status: 'partial', gateClass: 'soft', evidence: 'Skill README summary omits both restore branches.' },\n      { protocolId: 'agent_cross_runtime', level: 'overlay', status: 'notApplicable', applicable: false, gateClass: 'soft', evidence: 'No agent file in the manifest.' },\n      { protocolId: 'feature_catalog_code', level: 'overlay', status: 'fail', gateClass: 'hard', evidence: 'Lifecycle page says every failed restore exits 1; status 3 exits 0.' },\n      { protocolId: 'playbook_capability', level: 'overlay', status: 'pending', gateClass: 'soft', evidence: 'Lifecycle manual scenario still to be compared.' }\n    ]\n  },\n  newFindingsRatio: 0.5, sessionId: 'fanout-dsh-1-179465212