{"type":"thinking","text":"The exhausted approaches section now huge (lines 69-156) with many bogus blocked entries from traceability. It may be okay but makes strategy bloat. We should avoid feeding traceability bullets to deadEnds for future. Use prose or table under `Traceability Checks`? The parser `extractSection` gets section content, `extractListItems` finds bullet lines. We used headings and bullet lists. For iteration 3, avoid bullets in traceability and ruled-out? Ruled out should be bullets; those are legitimate and will be added. It builds exhausted from all iteration ruledOut and deadEnds. It will keep adding. It's not a correctness issue for review. The strategy is machine-managed partly.\n\nCould clean the bogus entries after final reducer? The reducer will re-add on each run. We could stop running reducer after final? But need final. It will re-add. We can leave; it doesn't affect convergence. The final report may show exhausted approaches from all. Not great but acceptable.\n\nNow iteration 3. Need findings:\nR3-P1-007: `archivedPaths` missing from docs. Primary maybe `.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/feature-catalog/retrieval/rg-archive-search.md:28`. It states \"In JSON... each row in results/counts... paths list stays plain strings. Without the flag none of these fields appear, and report shape unchanged.\" The code always adds `archivedPaths` to path records, even without flag. This is direct contradiction. P1. Also retrieval-conventions line 84 and search.md line 116, presentation line 120, root README 1205, skill README 332, README.txt line 105. Use primary feature page.\nR3-P1-008: `suggest-subtracks` non-NNN-slug refusal missing. Primary `folder-structure.md:141` says no map in three cases. Code has fourth. Also feature page line 30. P1 or P2? It is a direct count contradiction and user may be surprised. The phase 009 goal likely has requirement. Let's read 009 goal criteria for exact text."}
