{"type":"tool_result","callId":"chatcmpl-tool-8e94ed90c08eff2f","status":"completed","result":"## 3. COMPLETION CRITERIA\n\n- [ ] `rg-wrapper.mjs path \"sk-doc agent template alignment\" --include-archive --json --limit 2` lists 2 `paths` and 2 `archivedPaths`, and a live-only phrase lists 0 `archivedPaths`\n- [ ] In a `mktemp` copy with an undeclared folder named like the top group, the map `suggest-subtracks.mjs --track demo` prints passes `relocate.mjs --map` with exit 1\n- [ ] With a packet named `003_under` in the track, `suggest-subtracks.mjs` names it, prints no map and exits 0\n- [ ] Under the pinned scoring regime, the system-spec-kit score for corpus row `rr-iter3-135` is the same with the reworded archive-search signal as with that signal removed, and `look up a phrase in the archived spec packets` returns system-spec-kit first\n- [ ] Under the pinned scoring regime, `suggest sub-tracks for the sk-code track` and its sk-git and sk-doc forms return system-spec-kit first, or T010 is marked `[B]` with the operator's answer recorded in section 4\n- [ ] The sk-code control prompt, `track down why a vitest suite is flaky` and `keep track of the open review comments` keep the top skill they had before the change, and every corpus row whose top skill changed is listed in section 4 as a sub-track or archive request\n- [ ] `scorer-eval-baseline-ratchet.vitest.ts` and `local-native-divergence-ratchet.vitest.ts` pass, and `git diff --stat` on `local-native-approved-divergences.json` prints nothing\n<!-- /ANCHOR:completion -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:log -->\n## 4. LOG\n=== 009 AC spec ===\nspecs/system-speckit/spec-folder-tooling/005-subtrack-proposal-and-archive-reach/009-proposal-search-and-routing/spec.md:105:| `C/spec/suggest-subtracks.mjs` | Modify | Group names avoid every existing folder of the track, and a packet not named `NNN-slug` is reported instead of mapped |\nspecs/system-speckit/spec-folder-tooling/005-subtrack-proposal-and-archive-reach/009-proposal-search-and-routing/spec.md:118:`RG` is `node C/retrieval/rg-wrapper.mjs`. `COUNT` is the first command below. It prints the number of listed paths and the number of `archivedPaths`. `SCORE` is the second, which prints one prompt's ranked skills under `PIN`. `PIN` is the pinned scoring regime the advisor's own baseline capture sets: `SKILL_ADVISOR_DISABLE_BUILTIN_SEMANTIC=1`, `SPECKIT_SKILL_ADVISOR_FORCE_LOCAL=1`, `VITEST=true` and an empty `SYSTEM_SKILL_ADVISOR_DB_DIR`.\nspecs/system-speckit/spec-folder-tooling/005-subtrack-proposal-and-archive-reach/009-proposal-search-and-routing/spec.md:121:RG path \"sk-doc agent template alignment\" --include-archive --json --limit 2 | node -e 'const r=JSON.parse(require(\"fs\").readFileSync(0,\"utf8\"));console.log(r.paths.length,(r.archivedPaths||[]).length)'\nspecs/system-speckit/spec-folder-tooling/005-subtrack-proposal-and-archive-reach/009-proposal-search-and-routing/spec.md:171:- Answered: the added field is `archivedPaths`, the name `COUNT` reads. T002 still lists the readers first, and a reader that already uses that name is raised as an open question before T005.\n[stderr]\ngrep: specs/system-speckit/spec-folder-tooling/005-subtrack-proposal-and-archive-reach/009-proposal-search-and-routing/acceptance-criteria.md: No such file or directory\n"}
