{"type":"tool_result","callId":"chatcmpl-tool-94ebeeaf51cd350a","status":"completed","result":"=== feature page line 28 ===\n    24\t### Archived hits\n    25\t\n    26\t`--include-archive` works with the structured, path-only and count recipes. It drops only the archive exclusion from the recipe, so the other guards and the file limit apply as before. A path counts as archived when one of its segments is exactly `z_archive`.\n    27\t\n    28\tIn human output each archived path ends with `[archived]`. In JSON the report carries `includeArchive: true`, and each row in `results` and in `counts` carries `archived: true` or `archived: false`. The `paths` list of the path-only recipe stays a list of plain strings. Without the flag none of these fields appear, and the report shape is unchanged.\n    29\t\n    30\t### Metadata lane\n    31\t\n    32\tThe flag also runs a second search for the same phrase over the `description.json` and `graph-metadata.json` files of archived packets. It is a separate ripgrep run, because one run cannot combine two output modes, and a caller cannot name it as a recipe.\n=== presentation line 120 ===\n   116\t| Normalized match class per the ranking tuple | `<matchClass>` — one of `exact`, `phrase-containment`, `query-containment`, `token-overlap`, `partial`, the same five labels the lookup emits |\n   117\t| Matches collapsed into the same file row | Append `(+N more in this file)` when `result.moreInFile` is greater than 0; omit it when the value is 0 |\n   118\t| Hidden files and matches | Render `record.hidden.files` and `record.hidden.matches` as `HIDDEN=<files>/<matches>`. The structured wrapper record uses `schemaVersion: 3` |\n   119\t| `record.includeArchive` is true and the path has a `z_archive` segment | Append `[archived]` to that row, after the `(+N more in this file)` suffix when both apply |\n   120\t| `result.archived` on a structured row, `archived` on a `record.counts` entry | The JSON field `archived`, `true` or `false`, present only when the run used `--include-archive`. Render `[archived]` when it is `true`. The path-only recipe returns plain path strings with no such field |\n   121\t| `record.jsonLane.paths` | The `json    : <count> archived metadata file(s)` line, then one `<path>  [archived]` line per `description.json` or `graph-metadata.json` of an archived packet that holds the phrase |\n   122\t\n   123\tRules:\n   124\t- Ripgrep produces matches, never a relevance ranking. Order rows with the Section 5 ranking tuple from `retrieval-conventions.md`: evidence field, then match class, then path and line. Never imply the tool ranked anything.\n   125\t- Do not invent a numeric score for this lane. There is none. A row carries a field, a class, a path and a line, and that is the whole record.\n   126\t- The `(+N more in this file)` suffix and the `HIDDEN` slot come from a `rg-wrapper.mjs` record with `schemaVersion: 3`, which keeps the first-ranked row per file and cuts at `--limit` files (default 20, `--limit 0` uncapped). Omit the suffix when `moreInFile` is 0.\n   127\t- `/speckit:search` runs the structured lane through the wrapper. When a phrase that starts with `--` forced the raw Section 2.1 recipe instead, there is no per-file shaping and no hidden count: omit the suffix and the `HIDDEN` slot, and report `RESULTS` as the matches rendered. Omit `HIDDEN` for path-only and count recipes too.\n   128\t- Render the `[archived]` label and the `json    :` section only for a run with `--include-archive`. Without the flag archived packets are not searched, the rows carry no `archived` field and the record has no `jsonLane`.\n   129\t- The `json    :` section comes from a second invocation that `--limit` does not bound. Print every path in `record.jsonLane.paths`, and count none of them in `RESULTS` or `HIDDEN`.\n   130\t- When only the `json    :` section matched, the record's outcome is `match` with exit `0` and no evidence rows. Render this display with `RESULTS=0` and the section, not the Section 4 no-hit.\n=== search.md 116 ===\n   110\tArchived packets are left out by default. Add `--include-archive` to any wrapper recipe to search them as well:\n   111\t\n   112\t```bash\n   113\tnode .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/retrieval/rg-wrapper.mjs path 'skill routing refactor' --include-archive\n   114\t```\n   115\t\n   116\tA phrase that only an archived packet holds exits `1` without the flag and `0` with it, and each archived path ends `[archived]`. The flag drops the `!**/z_archive/**` glob from the recipe and marks every printed hit under a `z_archive` segment with `[archived]`. The JSON rows of the structured and count recipes carry `archived: true|false`. A second invocation then lists the `description.json` and `graph-metadata.json` files of archived packets that hold the phrase, under a `json    :` section, and the exit is `0` when either lane matches. The mode is opt-in only. `/speckit:resume` excludes archives and has no such flag, and the trigger-index lane never reads them.\n   117\t\n   118\t1. Resolve the search roots. Narrow by path, never by pattern: `specs .skilled` for everything, `specs/<track>` for one track, `specs/<track>/<sub-track>` for one declared sub-track, `specs/<track>/<NNN-name>` for one packet, `specs/<track>/<sub-track>/<NNN-name>` for a packet inside a sub-track, `specs/<track>/<NNN-name>/<NNN-child-name>` for one phase child. `--packet <specFolder>` replaces the roots with that path.\n=== README.txt 105 ===\n   100\t| Free-text evidence | default | `rg-wrapper.mjs structured`, which runs the `retrieval-conventions.md` Section 2.1 recipe |\n   101\t| Which files mention it | `--paths` | Path-only recipe, Section 2.2 |\n   102\t| How many times | `--count` | Count recipe, Section 2.3 |\n   103\t| Archived packets too | `--include-archive` | Any `rg-wrapper.mjs` recipe (`structured`, `path` or `count`) without the `!**/z_archive/**` glob, plus a second invocation over the `description.json` and `graph-metadata.json` files of archived packets |\n   104\t\n   105\tArchived packets are left out by default. With `--include-archive` the wrapper marks each archived path `[archived]`, the JSON rows of the structured and count recipes carry `archived: true` or `archived: false`, and the archived metadata files that hold the phrase are listed under a `json    :` section. The exit is `0` when either invocation matches. The trigger-index lane never reads archives, and `/speckit:resume` has no such flag.\n   106\t\n   107\tThe `rg-wrapper.mjs` structured lane keeps the highest-ranked row per file, and `/speckit:search` runs its default lane through it. The wrapper's `--limit` defaults to 20 files, and `--limit 0` is uncapped. JSON uses `schemaVersion: 3` and reports `moreInFile`, `matchCount`, `fileCount`, `hidden: { files, matches }`, `limit` and `truncated`. The path-only and count recipes take the same limit and report the files they hid.\n   108\t\n"}
