{"type":"tool_result","callId":"chatcmpl-tool-92ae4355da594f18","status":"completed","result":".skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/README.md:79:+-- relocate.mjs                 # Move, renumber or re-parent packets and update every store\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/README.md:120:| `relocate.mjs` | Moves, renumbers or re-parents spec packets from `--map <file.json>`, `--from` with `--to`, or `--renumber <folder>`, and leaves every store that records a packet path agreeing with the new place. Preflight refuses a destination collision, a taken number (archived siblings count), a track left mixed, a destination deeper than one sub-track, a name that is not `NNN-slug`, a path outside `specs/` or through a link, and uncommitted changes on a path the run would move or rewrite, all before the first write. It then moves each folder (`git mv` when tracked), drops and adds phase-parent `children_ids` for the ids the map names, rewrites every whole old id under `specs/` and recomputes relative markdown links, and drives `migrate-generated-json --only`, `repair-derived.cjs`, `refresh-track-roots.mjs`, `cite-drift-scan.mjs --rebuild-redirects` and `generate-trigger-index.mjs`. Each applied move is appended to `sk-doc/shared/scripts/relocation-ledger.json`, and the run closes with `sweep-track-roots.mjs` and `validate.sh --strict` on each moved packet. A moved path named in `.skilled/bin/lib/compiled-route-layout.cjs` or `.github/workflows/*` is reported and fails the run, and is never rewritten. `--declare-subtrack <track>/<name>` writes a sub-track's `description.json`, `graph-metadata.json` and `z_archive/.gitkeep`. Dry run by default (exits 1 when work is found); `--apply` writes; exit 2 on a refusal or a failed step, and exit 3 when every step and the close sweep landed and only a moved packet's own validation failed. A rerun after status 3 finds nothing to do; a second `--apply` of an applied map also finds nothing to do, and rerunning a map that stopped part-way finishes it. |\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/feature-catalog/tooling-and-scripts/spec-packet-relocation.md:3:description: \"Moves, renumbers and re-parents spec packets and rewrites every store that records the packet path, as a dry run unless --apply is passed.\"\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/feature-catalog/tooling-and-scripts/spec-packet-relocation.md:9:  - \"re-parent packets into a sub-track\"\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/feature-catalog/tooling-and-scripts/spec-packet-relocation.md:17:Moves, renumbers and re-parents spec packets and rewrites every store that records the packet path, as a dry run unless --apply is passed.\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/feature-catalog/tooling-and-scripts/spec-packet-relocation.md:44:3. References to the old path are rewritten in the text files under `specs/`, and a phase parent's `children_ids` drops or adds the moved child. An old id is matched as a whole path, so a longer id that starts with it is left alone.\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/feature-catalog/tooling-and-scripts/spec-packet-relocation.md:91:| `.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/tests/relocate.vitest.ts` | Vitest | Covers move, renumber, re-parent, sub-track declaration, the refusals, the dry-run exit status and a repeated apply |\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/changelog/v2.13.0.0.md:3:description: \"One command moves, renumbers or re-parents a spec packet and fixes every record of its path. A new tool proposes sub-tracks and every sub-track gets its own archive. Search and validation can reach archived packets on request.\"\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/changelog/v2.13.0.0.md:36:- **One command moves a packet.** `relocate.mjs` moves, renumbers and re-parents packets. It rewrites every record of the path. <!-- section: Moving Packets -->\n"}
