{"type":"tool_result","callId":"chatcmpl-tool-86ccdb300ec54725","status":"completed","result":"=== playbook 492 test sources ===\n    25\tOperators run the exact prompt and command sequence for `492` and confirm each outcome without contradictory evidence.\n    26\t\n    27\t- Objective: Prove that `relocate.mjs` prints a complete plan and writes nothing without `--apply`, refuses a destination number that an archived packet holds, and moves the folders when `--apply` is passed in a throwaway copy.\n    28\t- Real user request: `The demo track has gaps in its packet numbers. Show me what a renumber would change before anything moves, then apply it in a throwaway copy and tell me where the packets ended up.`\n    29\t- Prompt: `Renumber the demo track with relocate.mjs in a throwaway copy of this checkout. Show the dry run first, confirm a move onto the archived number 002 is refused, then apply the renumber and report where each packet landed. Return PASS or FAIL with the copy path and the exit codes.`\n    30\t- Expected execution process: Copy the checkout without its `specs/` tree into the operating-system temp directory, build a small `demo` track there, commit it, run the dry runs and the refused move, apply the renumber, list the folders and rerun the dry run.\n    31\t- Expected signals: The dry runs exit `1` and print `relocate: dry run, nothing written (pass --apply to write)`. The refused move exits `2` and prints `relocate: nothing was written`. The applied run prints `relocate: applied 2 move(s)`, and the rerun prints `relocate: no moves to make; nothing to do` with exit `0`.\n    32\t- Desired user-visible outcome: A concise `PASS` with the copy path and the exit codes, or a `FAIL` that names the first violated check.\n    33\t- Pass/fail: PASS if every condition in Section 3 Pass / Fail holds, FAIL if any one does not.\n    34\t\n   230\t\n   231\t1. A dry run that prints `relocate: refused: ... has uncommitted changes` means step 3 did not commit the fixture. Run `git status --short specs` in the copy and commit what it lists.\n   232\t2. A `missing tool:` or `run this from the repository root` message means the command did not run from the copy root, or step 1 did not copy `.skilled`. Confirm `pwd -P` prints the `RELOCATE_COPY` path.\n   233\t3. A `step <name>: FAILED` line names the stage that stopped the applied run. The script prints `Rerun the same map to finish it`, so read the failure text, fix its cause in the copy and repeat step 7.\n   234\t4. If a live packet lands on `002`, read `renumberEntries` in `runtime/cli/spec/relocate.mjs`, which counts the numbers held in `z_archive/` as taken.\n   235\t5. Run `npx vitest run runtime/cli/tests/relocate.vitest.ts` from `.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit` and read its first failing assertion before changing this scenario.\n   236\t\n   237\t---\n   238\t\n   239\t## 4. SOURCE FILES\n   240\t\n   241\t### Playbook Sources\n   242\t\n   243\t| File | Role |\n   244\t|---|---|\n   245\t| [manual-testing-playbook.md](../manual-testing-playbook.md) | Root directory page and scenario registration |\n   246\t| [spec-packet-relocation.md](../../feature-catalog/tooling-and-scripts/spec-packet-relocation.md) | Matching current-state feature reference |\n   247\t\n   248\t### Implementation And Test Anchors\n   249\t\n   250\t| File | Role |\n   251\t|---|---|\n   252\t| `.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/relocate.mjs` | Plan builder, refusals, the applied steps and the closing sweep and validation |\n   253\t| `.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/lib/track-roots.mjs` | Track and sub-track layout the plan is checked against |\n   254\t| `.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/tests/relocate.vitest.ts` | Move, renumber, re-parent, refusal and idempotence cases |\n   255\t\n   256\tProvenance: manual only - node .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/relocate.mjs --renumber demo\n   257\t\n   258\t---\n   259\t\n   260\t## 5. SOURCE METADATA\n   261\t\n   262\t- Group: Tooling and Scripts\n   263\t- Playbook ID: 492\n   264\t- Canonical root source: `manual-testing-playbook.md`\n   265\t- Feature file path: `tooling-and-scripts/spec-packet-relocation.md`\n=== playbook root version ===\n     1\t---\n     2\ttitle: \"Spec Kit: Manual Testing Playbook\"\n     3\tdescription: \"Operator-facing reference combining the manual testing directory, integrated review/orchestration guidance, execution expectations, and per-feature validation files for the system-spec-kit engine.\"\n     4\tlast_updated: \"2026-11-13\"\n     5\tversion: 2.1.25.0\n     6\t---\n     7\t\n=== feature catalog root version ===\n     1\t---\n     2\ttitle: \"Spec Kit: Feature Catalog\"\n     3\tdescription: \"Unified reference combining the complete current feature inventory for the system-spec-kit engine after the memory server was removed.\"\n     4\ttrigger_phrases:\n     5\t  - \"spec kit feature catalog\"\n     6\t  - \"spec kit features\"\n     7\t  - \"spec kit feature inventory\"\n     8\t  - \"what does spec kit do\"\n     9\t  - \"spec kit capability inventory\"\n    10\tlast_updated: \"2026-11-13\"\n    11\tversion: 2.1.30.0\n    12\t---\n    13\t\n"}
