.env.example`, AGENTS.md, many presentation assets, `changelog`, reference memory/trigger-config, `rg-lane.mjs`, `validate-archive-recursive.vitest.ts`, etc. The scope is 74 files but we only read a subset. The review focus is docs; but the coverage gate may require all files? The manifest is 74 files. We need at least consider each category. We can say not all 74 read; review focus concentrated. But the completion criteria say scope exactly manifest. The evaluation may not inspect our review coverage, but we should be honest. We can list unreviewed surfaces as edge case, and in iteration 5 maybe scan the manifest for docs we didn't read. The user wants which docs need no change. We can classify:\n- `.env.example` no change (no env behavior changed).\n- `AGENTS.md` no change (not tied to relocation/archive).\n- presentation assets for create/deep commands? They might mention subtrack option C? The focus says command docs and presentation assets against sk-create-command, and \"reworded archive signal.\" We haven't checked `.skilled/commands/deep/assets/...` or `create-*presentation`. The manifest includes many presentation assets. Some might be stale regarding subtrack option C or archive signal. The goal says reviewer B findings 1-5 were handed to 008 session, not planned; those likely concern hub vocabulary. But the user focus says docs stale against 006-010 behavior. We should inspect presentation assets for \"archive\" and \"subtrack\" mentions. Use grep. Also `speckit-plan-presentation`, `speckit-complete-presentation`, `speckit-implement.yaml`, `search-presentation`. The manifest includes them. We should see if they mention subtrack/relocate/archive. If not, no change. Let's scan."}
