r B findings out of scope). But the review focus says \"command docs and presentation assets against sk-create-command\". Hmm.\n\nGiven scope and time, iteration 5 can note this as an edge case / not finding because reviewer B 1-5 are handed off and not planned (Q013). The prompt says \"reviewer B findings 1 to 5 concern the hub vocabulary packet on another session's branch.\" They are not in scope. We can cite D5 and Q013. Good.\n\nWe need maybe inspect `.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/workflows/quick-reference.md` and `worked-examples.md` for stale behavior. We saw they updated option C, but `quick-reference` line 295 \"Next spec number\" maybe no. It has create phase commands. `worked-examples` maybe no relocation. Could say no change.\n\n`references/retrieval/retrieval-conventions.md` line 84 missing archivedPaths (P1 finding). `search.md` line 116 missing. `README.txt` line 105 missing. Good.\n\n`references/memory/trigger-config.md` line 142 has option C wording \"new or existing sub-track\" without whole-track. Could be consistent with reviewer B. It's in manifest. Is that a docs gap? The phase 002 changed option C, and trigger-config line 142 says \"Use a related folder, phase child, new or existing sub-track...\" It doesn't mention whole-track map. But maybe that's fine because it's a short phrase. The quick-reference detailed rule says whole-track. Not a bug.\n\n`runtime/lib/search/README.md` maybe mentions archivedPaths? Let's check."}
