{"type":"tool_result","callId":"chatcmpl-tool-9d1a2f4af9775d63","status":"completed","result":"=== search README archive refs ===\n150:| `isGeneratedMetadataZExclusionEnabled()` | Function | Whether `z-future` segments are excluded from generated metadata (`SPECKIT_GENERATED_METADATA_Z_EXCLUSION`). `z_archive` stays in. |\n=== rg-flood-control archive refs ===\n69:- [rg-archive-search.md](rg-archive-search.md) - Covers the `--include-archive` mode of the same wrapper.\n=== spec validation archive refs ===\n2:title: \"495 -- Spec validation of archived packets\"\n3:description: \"This scenario validates archive-aware validation for `495`. It focuses on validate.sh --recursive visiting an archived packet only when --include-archive is passed, and refusing that flag without --recursive.\"\n7:# 495 -- Spec validation of archived packets\n9:This document captures the scratch-directory manual validation contract for `validate.sh --recursive --include-archive`.\n15:This scenario validates archive-aware validation for `495`. It focuses on `validate.sh --recursive` visiting an archived packet only when `--include-archive` is passed, and refusing that flag without `--recursive`. The fixture track lives in a scratch directory under the operating-system temp directory. The scenario never validates or writes this checkout's `specs/` tree.\n19:A recursive run walks a track's live packets and stops at `z_archive/`. That keeps a normal gate fast and free of old findings, but it also means nothing checks an archived packet after a move or a restore. The flag adds the packets in the `z_archive/` of the folder given and, for a track root, of each declared sub-track.\n27:- Objective: Prove that a recursive validation of a track reports its live packets only, that the same run with `--include-archive` also reports the archived packet, and that `--include-archive` without `--recursive` is refused with exit `2`.\n28:- Real user request: `Validate the demo track again, and this time include the archived packets. Show me which folders were checked.`\n29:- Prompt: `Validate the demo track with validate.sh --recursive, first without and then with --include-archive, and list the folders each run checked. Confirm the flag is refused without --recursive. Return PASS or FAIL with the folder lists and the exit codes.`\n30:- Expected execution process: Build a track with three live packets and one archived packet in a scratch directory, list the `Folder:` lines of a recursive run, repeat with `--include-archive`, then pass the flag alone.\n31:- Expected signals: The recursive run prints four `Folder:` lines, the track and its three live packets. The archive run prints five, the fifth ending in `specs/demo/z_archive/002-old`. The flag alone prints `ERROR: --include-archive requires --recursive` and exits `2`.\n42:Validate the demo track with validate.sh --recursive, first without and then with --include-archive, and list the folders each run checked. Confirm the flag is refused without --recursive. Return PASS or FAIL with the folder lists and the exit codes.\n50:   export VALIDATE_ARCHIVE_DEMO=\"$(cd \"$(mktemp -d \"${TMPDIR:-/tmp}/validate-archive-manual.XXXXXX\")\" && pwd -P)\"\n54:2. Build a `demo` track with three live packets and one archived packet. Each packet holds a bare `spec.md` and its two metadata files.\n58:   mkdir -p specs/demo/001-alpha specs/demo/004-beta specs/demo/006-gamma specs/demo/z_archive/002-old\n64:   printf '# Old\\n\\nLedger reconciliation, first attempt.\\n' > specs/demo/z_archive/002-old/spec.md\n68:   printf '{\"level\":\"task\",\"specFolder\":\"demo/z_archive/002-old\",\"description\":\"Ledger reconciliation, first attempt.\"}\\n' > specs/demo/z_archive/002-old/description.json\n72:   printf '{\"schema_version\":1,\"packet_id\":\"demo/z_archive/002-old\",\"spec_folder\":\"demo/z_archive/002-old\",\"parent_id\":\"demo\",\"children_ids\":[]}\\n' > specs/demo/z_archive/002-old/graph-metadata.json\n82:4. Repeat with `--include-archive`.\n85:   bash .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/validate.sh \"$VALIDATE_ARCHIVE_DEMO/specs/demo\" --recursive --include-archive 2>&1 | grep \"Folder:\"\n93:   bash .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/validate.sh \"$VALIDATE_ARCHIVE_DEMO/specs/demo\" --recursive --include-archive --quiet\n100:   bash .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/validate.sh \"$VALIDATE_ARCHIVE_DEMO/specs/demo\" --include-archive\n121:Step 4 prints the same four lines and a fifth for the archived packet.\n128:  Folder: <demo>/specs/demo/z_archive/002-old\n150:ERROR: --include-archive requires --recursive\n151:Usage: ./validate.sh <folder-path> --recursive --include-archive\n160:- **Pass**: step 3 prints four `Folder:` lines and none holds `z_archive`, step 4 prints five and the fifth ends in `specs/demo/z_archive/002-old`, step 5 prints four result lines for the first run and five for the second, and step 6 prints `ERROR: --include-archive requires --recursive` with `FLAG_ALONE_EXIT=2`.\n161:- **Fail**: the run without the flag reports a `z_archive` folder, the run with the flag does not report `002-old`, the two runs print the same number of result lines, or the flag alone is accepted.\n165:1. If step 4 prints four lines only, confirm the archived packet from step 2 holds its spec document in the scratch directory and that `z_archive` is a real folder. A `z_archive` that is a symbolic link is not followed.\n166:2. If step 3 already lists the archived packet, read the recursive folder discovery in `runtime/cli/spec/validate.sh` and compare it with the `--include-archive` text in `validate.sh --help`.\n168:4. Run `npx vitest run runtime/cli/tests/validate-archive-recursive.vitest.ts` from `.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit` and read its first failing assertion before changing this scenario.\n185:| `.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/validate.sh` | Recursive folder discovery, the `--include-archive` flag and its refusal without `--recursive` |\n186:| `.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/tests/validate-archive-recursive.vitest.ts` | Archived track packet, archived sub-track packet, archived phase, flag refusal and linked archive cases |\n188:Provenance: manual only - bash .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/validate.sh \"$VALIDATE_ARCHIVE_DEMO/specs/demo\" --recursive --include-archive\n197:- Feature file path: `tooling-and-scripts/spec-validation-archive-reach.md`\n"}
