{"type":"tool_result","callId":"chatcmpl-tool-b364cc555790bcac","status":"completed","result":"=== quick-reference subtrack/archive ===\n139:# In a declared sub-track, numbered from 001 inside it:\n231:| `archived` | Historical record | 5 (do not reuse) |\n267:**Sub-Tracks:** If the work belongs to a track that is grouped into sub-tracks, prefer Option C and place the packet in the sub-track that fits. If the track's packets have grown into clusters and no sub-track fits, prefer Option C and propose a new sub-track as a whole-track map (`folder-structure.md` §2, When to Propose a Sub-Track). A sub-track is a proposal the operator approves, never a move made silently.\n279:- **Option C:** Use another existing packet — a related spec when it is a better scope match, a specific child under an existing phase parent, a related standard packet decomposed into phases when it meets both phase thresholds, a sub-track of the track (an existing one, or a new one proposed as a whole-track map when the track's packets have grown into clusters), or a series parent when the work is a different change to the same artifact as an existing packet in the same track (phase-definitions.md §2).\n282:**Recommendation priority:** `C` for a distinct related workstream in an existing or qualifying phased packet, including a series parent; otherwise `A` when the current packet fits; otherwise `C` for another related packet or a sub-track of the track, existing or newly proposed; `B` only for new/unrelated work; `D` is never the default.\n=== worked examples ===\n71:AI: Spec folder? A) Existing B) New (new or unrelated work only) C) Related (Use a related folder, phase child, new or existing sub-track, or a series parent for a different change to the same artifact as an existing packet in the same track) D) Skip\n=== trigger config ===\n142:# AI then asks: \"Spec Folder (required): A) Existing | B) New (new or unrelated work only) | C) Related (Use a related folder, phase child, new or existing sub-track, or a series parent for a different change to the same artifact as an existing packet in the same track) | D) Skip\"\n"}
